    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-8d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8D Meaning of claim period",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-8d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a claim period is:\n\n(a) the 2000-2001 financial year and each later financial year; or\n\n(b) if the Minister determines in writing another period—the\nother period.\n\n(2) The Minister may determine different periods under\nparagraph (1)(b) in respect of:\n\n(a) one or more universal service subsidies; or\n\n(b) the digital data cost of one or more digital data service\nproviders.\n\n(3) A period determined by the Minister under paragraph (1)(b) must\nnot be a part of more than one financial year.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            7\n\n(4) If the Minister determines a period under paragraph (1)(b), the\ndetermination may modify the way this Part applies to carriers and\ncarriage service providers. The modifications may include\nadditions, omissions and substitutions.\n\n(5) A determination under paragraph (1)(b) is a disallowable\ninstrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a claim period is:\n\n(a) the 2000-2001 financial year and each later financial year; or\n\n(b) if the Minister determines in writing another period—the\nother period.\n\n(2) The Minister may determine different periods under\nparagraph (1)(b) in respect of:\n\n(a) one or more universal service subsidies; or\n\n(b) the digital data cost of one or more digital data service\nproviders.\n\n(3) A period determined by the Minister under paragraph (1)(b) must\nnot be a part of more than one financial year.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            7\n\n(4) If the Minister determines a period under paragraph (1)(b), the\ndetermination may modify the way this Part applies to carriers and\ncarriage service providers. The modifications may include\nadditions, omissions and substitutions.\n\n(5) A determination under paragraph (1)(b) is a disallowable\ninstrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-8d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-8d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-8d-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-8d-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-8d-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "650c51d864a2820945c27e4194c4fa57d7600c338286c1d07bbbaa9d91d5768e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-8d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8D Meaning of claim period",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a claim period is:\n\n(a) the 2000-2001 financial year and each later financial year; or\n\n(b) if the Minister determines in writing another period—the\nother period.\n\n(2) The Minister may determine different periods under\nparagraph (1)(b) in respect of:\n\n(a) one or more universal service subsidies; or\n\n(b) the digital data cost of one or more digital data service\nproviders.\n\n(3) A period determined by the Minister under paragraph (1)(b) must\nnot be a part of more than one financial year.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            7\n\n(4) If the Minister determines a period under paragraph (1)(b), the\ndetermination may modify the way this Part applies to carriers and\ncarriage service providers. The modifications may include\nadditions, omissions and substitutions.\n\n(5) A determination under paragraph (1)(b) is a disallowable\ninstrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901."
    },
