    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 Universal service obligation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, the universal service obligation is the\nobligation:\n\n(a) to ensure that standard telephone services are reasonably\naccessible to all people in Australia on an equitable basis,\nwherever they reside or carry on business; and\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999\n\n8            Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No.\n2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n\n(b) to ensure that payphones are reasonably accessible to all\npeople in Australia on an equitable basis, wherever they\nreside or carry on business; and\n\n(c) to ensure that prescribed carriage services are reasonably\naccessible to all people in Australia on an equitable basis,\nwherever they reside or carry on business.\n\n(2) To the extent necessary to achieve the obligation mentioned in\nsubsection (1), the universal service obligation includes:\n\n(a) the supply of standard telephone services to people in\nAustralia on request; and\n\n(b) the supply, installation and maintenance of payphones in\nAustralia; and\n\n(c) the supply of prescribed carriage services to people in\nAustralia on request.\n\n(3) The Minister may make a written determination that the universal\nservice obligation includes the supply, installation and maintenance\nof payphones at specified locations in Australia. The determination\nhas effect accordingly and a copy of the determination must be\npublished in the Gazette.\n\n(4) An obligation does not arise under paragraph (2)(a) in relation to\nparticular equipment, goods or services the supply of which is\ntreated under section 9E as the supply of a standard telephone\nservice if the customer concerned requests not to be supplied with\nthe equipment, goods or services.\n\n(5) An obligation does not arise under paragraph (2)(c) in relation to\nparticular equipment, goods or services the supply of which is\ntreated under section 9F as the supply of a prescribed carriage\nservice if the customer concerned requests not to be supplied with\nthe equipment, goods or services.\n\n(6) To avoid doubt, an obligation arising under paragraph (2)(a) in\nrelation to customer equipment requires the customer concerned to\nbe given the option of hiring the equipment.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, the universal service obligation is the\nobligation:\n\n(a) to ensure that standard telephone services are reasonably\naccessible to all people in Australia on an equitable basis,\nwherever they reside or carry on business; and\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999\n\n8            Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No.\n2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n\n(b) to ensure that payphones are reasonably accessible to all\npeople in Australia on an equitable basis, wherever they\nreside or carry on business; and\n\n(c) to ensure that prescribed carriage services are reasonably\naccessible to all people in Australia on an equitable basis,\nwherever they reside or carry on business.\n\n(2) To the extent necessary to achieve the obligation mentioned in\nsubsection (1), the universal service obligation includes:\n\n(a) the supply of standard telephone services to people in\nAustralia on request; and\n\n(b) the supply, installation and maintenance of payphones in\nAustralia; and\n\n(c) the supply of prescribed carriage services to people in\nAustralia on request.\n\n(3) The Minister may make a written determination that the universal\nservice obligation includes the supply, installation and maintenance\nof payphones at specified locations in Australia. The determination\nhas effect accordingly and a copy of the determination must be\npublished in the Gazette.\n\n(4) An obligation does not arise under paragraph (2)(a) in relation to\nparticular equipment, goods or services the supply of which is\ntreated under section 9E as the supply of a standard telephone\nservice if the customer concerned requests not to be supplied with\nthe equipment, goods or services.\n\n(5) An obligation does not arise under paragraph (2)(c) in relation to\nparticular equipment, goods or services the supply of which is\ntreated under section 9F as the supply of a prescribed carriage\nservice if the customer conc",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-9-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-9-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-9-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-9-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-9-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-9-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e8dbeb1726786fed044ca29a46b87aad094e2dc6a5c2fa40065033a00c259329"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 Universal service obligation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, the universal service obligation is the\nobligation:\n\n(a) to ensure that standard telephone services are reasonably\naccessible to all people in Australia on an equitable basis,\nwherever they reside or carry on business; and\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999\n\n8            Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No.\n2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n\n(b) to ensure that payphones are reasonably accessible to all\npeople in Australia on an equitable basis, wherever they\nreside or carry on business; and\n\n(c) to ensure that prescribed carriage services are reasonably\naccessible to all people in Australia on an equitable basis,\nwherever they reside or carry on business.\n\n(2) To the extent necessary to achieve the obligation mentioned in\nsubsection (1), the universal service obligation includes:\n\n(a) the supply of standard telephone services to people in\nAustralia on request; and\n\n(b) the supply, installation and maintenance of payphones in\nAustralia; and\n\n(c) the supply of prescribed carriage services to people in\nAustralia on request.\n\n(3) The Minister may make a written determination that the universal\nservice obligation includes the supply, installation and maintenance\nof payphones at specified locations in Australia. The determination\nhas effect accordingly and a copy of the determination must be\npublished in the Gazette.\n\n(4) An obligation does not arise under paragraph (2)(a) in relation to\nparticular equipment, goods or services the supply of which is\ntreated under section 9E as the supply of a standard telephone\nservice if the customer concerned requests not to be supplied with\nthe equipment, goods or services.\n\n(5) An obligation does not arise under paragraph (2)(c) in relation to\nparticular equipment, goods or services the supply of which is\ntreated under section 9F as the supply of a prescribed carriage\nservice if the customer concerned requests not to be supplied with\nthe equipment, goods or services.\n\n(6) To avoid doubt, an obligation arising under paragraph (2)(a) in\nrelation to customer equipment requires the customer concerned to\nbe given the option of hiring the equipment."
    },
