    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-9b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9B What is a service obligation?",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-9b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Unless the Minister makes a determination under subsection (2),\neach of the following is a service obligation:\n\n(a) the obligation referred to in paragraph 9(1)(a) (dealing with\nthe standard telephone services);\n\n(b) the obligation referred to in paragraph 9(1)(b) (dealing with\npayphones);\n\n(c) the obligation referred to in paragraph 9(1)(c) (dealing with\nprescribed carriage services).\n\n(2) The Minister may determine in writing the service obligations by\ndividing the universal service obligation in another way.\n\n(3) The determination must also specify, in respect of each service\nobligation, what must be supplied or done in order to fulfil the\nservice obligation.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Unless the Minister makes a determination under subsection (2),\neach of the following is a service obligation:\n\n(a) the obligation referred to in paragraph 9(1)(a) (dealing with\nthe standard telephone services);\n\n(b) the obligation referred to in paragraph 9(1)(b) (dealing with\npayphones);\n\n(c) the obligation referred to in paragraph 9(1)(c) (dealing with\nprescribed carriage services).\n\n(2) The Minister may determine in writing the service obligations by\ndividing the universal service obligation in another way.\n\n(3) The determination must also specify, in respect of each service\nobligation, what must be supplied or done in order to fulfil the\nservice obligation.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-9b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-9b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-9b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "19c7279934413f98884a59a948f024b9bb862b810539ef4e7220ef5252c609d0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-9b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9B What is a service obligation?",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Unless the Minister makes a determination under subsection (2),\neach of the following is a service obligation:\n\n(a) the obligation referred to in paragraph 9(1)(a) (dealing with\nthe standard telephone services);\n\n(b) the obligation referred to in paragraph 9(1)(b) (dealing with\npayphones);\n\n(c) the obligation referred to in paragraph 9(1)(c) (dealing with\nprescribed carriage services).\n\n(2) The Minister may determine in writing the service obligations by\ndividing the universal service obligation in another way.\n\n(3) The determination must also specify, in respect of each service\nobligation, what must be supplied or done in order to fulfil the\nservice obligation.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
    },
