    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-9e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9E Supply of standard telephone services",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-9e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A reference in this Part to the supply of a standard telephone\nservice includes a reference to the supply of:\n\n(a) if the regulations prescribe customer equipment for the\npurposes of this paragraph—whichever of the following is\napplicable:\n\n(i) that customer equipment;\n\n(ii) if other customer equipment is supplied, instead of the\nfirst-mentioned customer equipment, in order to comply\nwith the Disability Discrimination Act 1992—that other\ncustomer equipment; and\n\n(b) if paragraph (a) does not apply—whichever of the following\nis applicable:\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            11\n\n(i) a telephone handset that does not have switching\nfunctions;\n\n(ii) if other customer equipment is supplied, instead of such\na handset, in order to comply with the Disability\nDiscrimination Act 1992—that other customer\nequipment; and\n\n(c) other goods of a kind specified in the regulations; and\n\n(d) services of a kind specified in the regulations;\nwhere the equipment, goods or services, as the case may be, are for\nuse in connection with the standard telephone service.\n\n(2) A reference in this Part to the supply of a standard telephone\nservice includes a reference to the supply, to a person with a\ndisability, of:\n\n(a) customer equipment of a kind specified in the regulations;\nand\n\n(b) other goods of a kind specified in the regulations; and\n\n(c) services of a kind specified in the regulations;\nwhere the equipment, goods or services, as the case may be, are for\nuse in connection with the standard telephone service.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A reference in this Part to the supply of a standard telephone\nservice includes a reference to the supply of:\n\n(a) if the regulations prescribe customer equipment for the\npurposes of this paragraph—whichever of the following is\napplicable:\n\n(i) that customer equipment;\n\n(ii) if other customer equipment is supplied, instead of the\nfirst-mentioned customer equipment, in order to comply\nwith the Disability Discrimination Act 1992—that other\ncustomer equipment; and\n\n(b) if paragraph (a) does not apply—whichever of the following\nis applicable:\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            11\n\n(i) a telephone handset that does not have switching\nfunctions;\n\n(ii) if other customer equipment is supplied, instead of such\na handset, in order to comply with the Disability\nDiscrimination Act 1992—that other customer\nequipment; and\n\n(c) other goods of a kind specified in the regulations; and\n\n(d) services of a kind specified in the regulations;\nwhere the equipment, goods or services, as the case may be, are for\nuse in connection with the standard telephone service.\n\n(2) A reference in this Part to the supply of a standard telephone\nservice includes a reference to the supply, to a person with a\ndisability, of:\n\n(a) customer equipment of a kind specified in the regulations;\nand\n\n(b) other goods of a kind specified in the regulations; and\n\n(c) services of a kind specified in the regulations;\nwhere the equipment, goods or services, as the case may be, are for\nuse in connection with the standard telephone service.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-9e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-9e-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ec0c74e2803eb2fbab9a4358d4c774d274f3c91f249fd384a5a5af2893e64665"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-9e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9E Supply of standard telephone services",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A reference in this Part to the supply of a standard telephone\nservice includes a reference to the supply of:\n\n(a) if the regulations prescribe customer equipment for the\npurposes of this paragraph—whichever of the following is\napplicable:\n\n(i) that customer equipment;\n\n(ii) if other customer equipment is supplied, instead of the\nfirst-mentioned customer equipment, in order to comply\nwith the Disability Discrimination Act 1992—that other\ncustomer equipment; and\n\n(b) if paragraph (a) does not apply—whichever of the following\nis applicable:\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            11\n\n(i) a telephone handset that does not have switching\nfunctions;\n\n(ii) if other customer equipment is supplied, instead of such\na handset, in order to comply with the Disability\nDiscrimination Act 1992—that other customer\nequipment; and\n\n(c) other goods of a kind specified in the regulations; and\n\n(d) services of a kind specified in the regulations;\nwhere the equipment, goods or services, as the case may be, are for\nuse in connection with the standard telephone service.\n\n(2) A reference in this Part to the supply of a standard telephone\nservice includes a reference to the supply, to a person with a\ndisability, of:\n\n(a) customer equipment of a kind specified in the regulations;\nand\n\n(b) other goods of a kind specified in the regulations; and\n\n(c) services of a kind specified in the regulations;\nwhere the equipment, goods or services, as the case may be, are for\nuse in connection with the standard telephone service."
    },
