        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-9h-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ead35818896bbadff9f88e2931fef3db93a05f1c1cce3350dbf778d7cc5bfec8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-9h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9H Effect of determination",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A determination under section 9G takes effect on the day specified\nin the determination. That day must not be before the day on which\nnotice of the determination is published in the Gazette.\n\n(2) If the determination is expressed to cease to have effect at a\nspecified time, the determination ceases to have effect at that time.\n\n(3) A variation or revocation of a determination under section 9G takes\neffect on the day specified for the purpose in the instrument of\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            13\nvariation or revocation. That day must not be before notice of the\ninstrument is published in the Gazette."
    },
