      "cml:integrityHash": "bd4faec3700dbd47cc56f97f095b24d7a320d7a61351f88167b4cb168b0b5226",
      "skos:note": "Definition of special digital data service"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-10e-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10E(3) Digital data services",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 19,
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of this Act, a special digital data service is a\ncarriage service that provides for a capability for the delivery of\ndigital data to an end-user broadly comparable to the\ncorresponding capability provided by a data channel with a data\ntransmission speed of 64 kilobits per second supplied to end-users\nas part of the designated basic rate ISDN service.\nDesignated basic rate ISDN service"
    },
