    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-10g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10G Supply of special digital data services",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-10g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A reference in this Part to the supply of a special digital data\nservice includes a reference to the supply of:\n\n(a) customer equipment of a kind specified in the regulations;\nand\n\n(b) other goods of a kind specified in the regulations; and\n\n(c) services of a kind specified in the regulations;\nwhere:\n\n(d) the equipment, goods or services, as the case may be, are for\nuse in connection with the special digital data service; and\n\n(e) the supply complies with such requirements, restrictions or\nconditions (if any) as are specified in the regulations.\n\n(2) Regulations made for the purposes of paragraph (1)(e) may require\nthat the supply of a specified kind of customer equipment is to be\nby way of hire. If those regulations impose such a requirement, this\nPart has effect, in relation to the customer equipment concerned, as\nif a reference to supply were a reference to supply by way of hire.\n\n(3) Regulations made for the purposes of paragraph (1)(e) may require\nthat specified customer equipment is to be supplied on the basis\nthat the customer concerned enters into a legally enforceable\nagreement containing such terms and conditions relating to the\nownership, possession, location, disposal or use of the equipment,\nas are specified in, or ascertained in accordance with, the\nregulations.\n\n(4) Subsections (2) and (3) do not, by implication, limit\nparagraph (1)(e).\nSubdivision B—Digital data service areas",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A reference in this Part to the supply of a special digital data\nservice includes a reference to the supply of:\n\n(a) customer equipment of a kind specified in the regulations;\nand\n\n(b) other goods of a kind specified in the regulations; and\n\n(c) services of a kind specified in the regulations;\nwhere:\n\n(d) the equipment, goods or services, as the case may be, are for\nuse in connection with the special digital data service; and\n\n(e) the supply complies with such requirements, restrictions or\nconditions (if any) as are specified in the regulations.\n\n(2) Regulations made for the purposes of paragraph (1)(e) may require\nthat the supply of a specified kind of customer equipment is to be\nby way of hire. If those regulations impose such a requirement, this\nPart has effect, in relation to the customer equipment concerned, as\nif a reference to supply were a reference to supply by way of hire.\n\n(3) Regulations made for the purposes of paragraph (1)(e) may require\nthat specified customer equipment is to be supplied on the basis\nthat the customer concerned enters into a legally enforceable\nagreement containing such terms and conditions relating to the\nownership, possession, location, disposal or use of the equipment,\nas are specified in, or ascertained in accordance with, the\nregulations.\n\n(4) Subsections (2) and (3) do not, by implication, limit\nparagraph (1)(e).\nSubdivision B—Digital data service areas",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-10g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-10g-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-10g-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-10g-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5a39f640a98ae04ea8102d457e6dbf822549de7cd82343a275ffe4e71ad039aa"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-10g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10G Supply of special digital data services",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 21,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A reference in this Part to the supply of a special digital data\nservice includes a reference to the supply of:\n\n(a) customer equipment of a kind specified in the regulations;\nand\n\n(b) other goods of a kind specified in the regulations; and\n\n(c) services of a kind specified in the regulations;\nwhere:\n\n(d) the equipment, goods or services, as the case may be, are for\nuse in connection with the special digital data service; and\n\n(e) the supply complies with such requirements, restrictions or\nconditions (if any) as are specified in the regulations.\n\n(2) Regulations made for the purposes of paragraph (1)(e) may require\nthat the supply of a specified kind of customer equipment is to be\nby way of hire. If those regulations impose such a requirement, this\nPart has effect, in relation to the customer equipment concerned, as\nif a reference to supply were a reference to supply by way of hire.\n\n(3) Regulations made for the purposes of paragraph (1)(e) may require\nthat specified customer equipment is to be supplied on the basis\nthat the customer concerned enters into a legally enforceable\nagreement containing such terms and conditions relating to the\nownership, possession, location, disposal or use of the equipment,\nas are specified in, or ascertained in accordance with, the\nregulations.\n\n(4) Subsections (2) and (3) do not, by implication, limit\nparagraph (1)(e).\nSubdivision B—Digital data service areas"
    },
