        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section sets out the arrangements for the fulfilment of the\nuniversal service obligation by universal service providers.\n\n(2) The default arrangements set out in Division 5 apply to each\nuniversal service area in respect of a service obligation.\n\n(3) If the Minister determines under section 11C, for a universal\nservice area in respect of a service obligation, that the obligation is\na contestable service obligation, then:\n\n(a) the default arrangements set out in Division 5 apply to the\narea; and\n\n(b) the standard contestability arrangements set out in Division 6\napply to the area in respect of the contestable service\nobligation.\n\n(4) If the Minister determines under Division 7 that alternative\narrangements apply to a universal service area in respect of a\nservice obligation (whether or not it is a contestable service\nobligation), then:\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            19\n\n(a) those alternative arrangements apply to the area; and\n\n(b) the default arrangements set out in Division 5 apply to the\narea except to the extent that the determination modifies the\nway those arrangements apply, or excludes them from\napplying, to the area.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section sets out the arrangements for the fulfilment of the\nuniversal service obligation by universal service providers.\n\n(2) The default arrangements set out in Division 5 apply to each\nuniversal service area in respect of a service obligation.\n\n(3) If the Minister determines under section 11C, for a universal\nservice area in respect of a service obligation, that the obligation is\na contestable service obligation, then:\n\n(a) the default arrangements set out in Division 5 apply to the\narea; and\n\n(b) the standard contestability arrangements set out in Division 6\napply to the area in respect of the contestable service\nobligation.\n\n(4) If the Minister determines under Division 7 that alternative\narrangements apply to a universal service area in respect of a\nservice obligation (whether or not it is a contestable service\nobligation), then:\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            19\n\n(a) those alternative arrangements apply to the area; and\n\n(b) the default arrangements set out in Division 5 apply to the\narea except to the extent that the determination modifies the\nway those arrangements apply, or excludes them from\napplying, to the area.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-11-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-11-ss-2"
