    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20(3) Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The current provider may, by written notice given to the former\nprovider, require the former provider to give to the current provider\nspecified information of the kind referred to in subsection (4). A\nnotice of this kind cannot be given more than 6 months after:\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            21\n\n(a) if subsection (1) applies—the later of the following days:\n\n(i) the day on which the current provider became a\nuniversal service provider for the relevant area; or\n\n(ii) the day on which the determination under section 12A\nwas made, or the approval under section 13B was given,\n(as the case may be) in respect of the current provider;\nor\n\n(b) if subsection (2) applies—the day on which the former\nprovider ceases to be a universal service provider for the\nrelevant area.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The current provider may, by written notice given to the former\nprovider, require the former provider to give to the current provider\nspecified information of the kind referred to in subsection (4). A\nnotice of this kind cannot be given more than 6 months after:\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            21\n\n(a) if subsection (1) applies—the later of the following days:\n\n(i) the day on which the current provider became a\nuniversal service provider for the relevant area; or\n\n(ii) the day on which the determination under section 12A\nwas made, or the approval under section 13B was given,\n(as the case may be) in respect of the current provider;\nor\n\n(b) if subsection (2) applies—the day on which the former\nprovider ceases to be a universal service provider for the\nrelevant area.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0f56c00e208f7c6d7af78d0b6aa38b9504397b2242c5e5bf70e3835670f2fa24",
      "skos:note": "Former provider must provide specified information to current provider within 6 months after certain events.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20(3) Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The current provider may, by written notice given to the former\nprovider, require the former provider to give to the current provider\nspecified information of the kind referred to in subsection (4). A\nnotice of this kind cannot be given more than 6 months after:\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            21\n\n(a) if subsection (1) applies—the later of the following days:\n\n(i) the day on which the current provider became a\nuniversal service provider for the relevant area; or\n\n(ii) the day on which the determination under section 12A\nwas made, or the approval under section 13B was given,\n(as the case may be) in respect of the current provider;\nor\n\n(b) if subsection (2) applies—the day on which the former\nprovider ceases to be a universal service provider for the\nrelevant area."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20-ss-3-norm",
