    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20(5) Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If a requirement made by a notice under subsection (3) is\nreasonable, the former provider must comply with the requirement\nas soon as practicable after receiving the notice. However, if the\nrequirement is unreasonable, the former provider does not have to\ncomply with it.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If a requirement made by a notice under subsection (3) is\nreasonable, the former provider must comply with the requirement\nas soon as practicable after receiving the notice. However, if the\nrequirement is unreasonable, the former provider does not have to\ncomply with it.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c6ea562425fb0858e3f0e0d22d0b50f44caf22b17bb4da7f8d1b42479dc6ea1d",
      "skos:note": "Former provider must comply with reasonable requirements after receiving notice.",
      "dc:description": "comply with requirement"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20(5) Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If a requirement made by a notice under subsection (3) is\nreasonable, the former provider must comply with the requirement\nas soon as practicable after receiving the notice. However, if the\nrequirement is unreasonable, the former provider does not have to\ncomply with it."
    },
