    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20-ss-6a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20(6A) Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20-ss-6a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(6A) If a former provider has been given notice of a requirement under\nsubsection (3), the ACA may, in writing, direct the former provider\nto comply with the requirement or with specified aspects of the\nrequirement. The former provider must comply with the direction.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "(6A) If a former provider has been given notice of a requirement under\nsubsection (3), the ACA may, in writing, direct the former provider\nto comply with the requirement or with specified aspects of the\nrequirement. The former provider must comply with the direction.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
