        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20-ss-6a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c5fbec861469c66e0d2d455410d9e22e0dc287e38df96c307771fc1c5e191cca",
      "skos:note": "Former provider must comply with direction from ACA."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20-ss-6a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20(6A) Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(6A) If a former provider has been given notice of a requirement under\nsubsection (3), the ACA may, in writing, direct the former provider\nto comply with the requirement or with specified aspects of the\nrequirement. The former provider must comply with the direction.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20-ss-6a-norm",
