      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n\n(6B) In deciding whether to give a direction under subsection (6A), the\nACA must consider whether the requirement under subsection (3)\nis reasonable.\n\n(7) A determination under subsection (6) is a disallowable instrument\nfor the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n\n(6B) In deciding whether to give a direction under subsection (6A), the\nACA must consider whether the requirement under subsection (3)\nis reasonable.\n\n(7) A determination under subsection (6) is a disallowable instrument\nfor the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
