      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Minister revokes a determination under section 11C, the\nMinister may determine in writing arrangements to deal with any\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            23\nissues of a transitional nature that may arise as a result of the\nrevocation.\n\n(2) A copy of a determination under subsection (1) must be published\nin the Gazette.",
