    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-11f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "11F Section 11C temporarily limited to pilot areas",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-11f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Until the Minister has done both of the following, the Minister can\nmake determinations under section 11C only in relation to pilot\nareas (as defined in subsection (2)):\n\n(a) received a comprehensive report, following a public inquiry\nby the ACA, on whether a net benefit has accrued from the\noperation, for a period not less than 12 months, of the\nstandard contestability arrangements in each of the pilot\nareas;\n\n(b) caused the report to be tabled in each House of the\nParliament within 10 sitting days of that House after the\nMinister receives the report.\n\n(2) A pilot area is an area determined in writing by the Minister for\nthe purposes of this section. The Minister may determine a\nmaximum of 2 pilot areas and cannot later change the boundaries\nof a pilot area.\n\n(3) Before the Minister can make any determination under section 11C\nin relation to a pilot area, the Minister must have determined under\nsection 9G one or more universal service areas that cover the\nwhole of the pilot area.\n\n(4) A copy of a determination under subsection (2) must be published\nin the Gazette.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Until the Minister has done both of the following, the Minister can\nmake determinations under section 11C only in relation to pilot\nareas (as defined in subsection (2)):\n\n(a) received a comprehensive report, following a public inquiry\nby the ACA, on whether a net benefit has accrued from the\noperation, for a period not less than 12 months, of the\nstandard contestability arrangements in each of the pilot\nareas;\n\n(b) caused the report to be tabled in each House of the\nParliament within 10 sitting days of that House after the\nMinister receives the report.\n\n(2) A pilot area is an area determined in writing by the Minister for\nthe purposes of this section. The Minister may determine a\nmaximum of 2 pilot areas and cannot later change the boundaries\nof a pilot area.\n\n(3) Before the Minister can make any determination under section 11C\nin relation to a pilot area, the Minister must have determined under\nsection 9G one or more universal service areas that cover the\nwhole of the pilot area.\n\n(4) A copy of a determination under subsection (2) must be published\nin the Gazette.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-11f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-11f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-11f-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-11f-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f480cabba39e5c3b00e4031d959aee9892b63f094ae50908be59f1953a2a30b2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-11f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11F Section 11C temporarily limited to pilot areas",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Until the Minister has done both of the following, the Minister can\nmake determinations under section 11C only in relation to pilot\nareas (as defined in subsection (2)):\n\n(a) received a comprehensive report, following a public inquiry\nby the ACA, on whether a net benefit has accrued from the\noperation, for a period not less than 12 months, of the\nstandard contestability arrangements in each of the pilot\nareas;\n\n(b) caused the report to be tabled in each House of the\nParliament within 10 sitting days of that House after the\nMinister receives the report.\n\n(2) A pilot area is an area determined in writing by the Minister for\nthe purposes of this section. The Minister may determine a\nmaximum of 2 pilot areas and cannot later change the boundaries\nof a pilot area.\n\n(3) Before the Minister can make any determination under section 11C\nin relation to a pilot area, the Minister must have determined under\nsection 9G one or more universal service areas that cover the\nwhole of the pilot area.\n\n(4) A copy of a determination under subsection (2) must be published\nin the Gazette."
    },
