    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-24",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-24"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\nNote:\nThese apply to each universal service area except to the extent that a\ndetermination of alternative arrangements modifies the way they\napply, or excludes them from applying, to the area (see subsection\n11(4)).\nSubdivision B—Primary universal service providers",
      "skos:definition": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\nNote:\nThese apply to each universal service area except to the extent that a\ndetermination of alternative arrangements modifies the way they\napply, or excludes them from applying, to the area (see subsection\n11(4)).\nSubdivision B—Primary universal service providers",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-24-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b8ea3e580f4bea85f57ea7c2e8636b8e98d2c1578b8f8a724cd93eae7fdcd0c7",
      "skos:note": "Applicable to each universal service area except to the extent that a determination of alternative arrangements modifies the way they apply, or excludes them from applying."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-24",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\nNote:\nThese apply to each universal service area except to the extent that a\ndetermination of alternative arrangements modifies the way they\napply, or excludes them from applying, to the area (see subsection\n11(4)).\nSubdivision B—Primary universal service providers"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-24-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-24"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12A Determination of primary universal service providers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may determine in writing that a specified carrier or\ncarriage service provider is the primary universal service provider\nfor a universal service area in respect of a service obligation.\n\n(2) The Minister may determine:\n\n(a) different primary universal service providers in respect of\ndifferent service obligations for the same universal service\narea; and\n\n(b) the same person as the primary universal service provider for\none or more universal service areas in respect of one or more\nservice obligations.\n\n(3) In exercising his or her powers under this section, the Minister\nmust ensure that at all times there is one primary universal service\nprovider, in respect of each service obligation, for each universal\nservice area.\n\n(4) In deciding whether to make a determination that a person is a\nprimary universal service provider, the Minister is limited to\nconsidering factors that are relevant to achieving the objects of this\nAct.\n\n(5) The Minister must give to the person and to the ACA a copy of the\ndetermination.\n\n(6) A determination under this section is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nNote:\nA determination that the Minister is taken to have made under this\nsection because of section 12D or 12E is not a disallowable instrument\n(see subsections 12D(2) and 12E(6)).\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            25",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may determine in writing that a specified carrier or\ncarriage service provider is the primary universal service provider\nfor a universal service area in respect of a service obligation.\n\n(2) The Minister may determine:\n\n(a) different primary universal service providers in respect of\ndifferent service obligations for the same universal service\narea; and\n\n(b) the same person as the primary universal service provider for\none or more universal service areas in respect of one or more\nservice obligations.\n\n(3) In exercising his or her powers under this section, the Minister\nmust ensure that at all times there is one primary universal service\nprovider, in respect of each service obligation, for each universal\nservice area.\n\n(4) In deciding whether to make a determination that a person is a\nprimary universal service provider, the Minister is limited to\nconsidering factors that are relevant to achieving the objects of this\nAct.\n\n(5) The Minister must give to the person and to the ACA a copy of the\ndetermination.\n\n(6) A determination under this section is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nNote:\nA determination that the Minister is taken to have made under this\nsection because of section 12D or 12E is not a disallowable instrument\n(see subsections 12D(2) and 12E(6)).\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            25",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "390d19e75ee34dfc658a84e2eb380473134fafa31b627d0edff5689404480f74"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12A Determination of primary universal service providers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may determine in writing that a specified carrier or\ncarriage service provider is the primary universal service provider\nfor a universal service area in respect of a service obligation.\n\n(2) The Minister may determine:\n\n(a) different primary universal service providers in respect of\ndifferent service obligations for the same universal service\narea; and\n\n(b) the same person as the primary universal service provider for\none or more universal service areas in respect of one or more\nservice obligations.\n\n(3) In exercising his or her powers under this section, the Minister\nmust ensure that at all times there is one primary universal service\nprovider, in respect of each service obligation, for each universal\nservice area.\n\n(4) In deciding whether to make a determination that a person is a\nprimary universal service provider, the Minister is limited to\nconsidering factors that are relevant to achieving the objects of this\nAct.\n\n(5) The Minister must give to the person and to the ACA a copy of the\ndetermination.\n\n(6) A determination under this section is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nNote:\nA determination that the Minister is taken to have made under this\nsection because of section 12D or 12E is not a disallowable instrument\n(see subsections 12D(2) and 12E(6)).\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            25"
    },
