    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12A(6) Determination of primary universal service providers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12a-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(6) A determination under this section is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nNote:\nA determination that the Minister is taken to have made under this\nsection because of section 12D or 12E is not a disallowable instrument\n(see subsections 12D(2) and 12E(6)).\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            25",
      "skos:definition": "(6) A determination under this section is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nNote:\nA determination that the Minister is taken to have made under this\nsection because of section 12D or 12E is not a disallowable instrument\n(see subsections 12D(2) and 12E(6)).\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            25",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a-ss-6-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "59da53a43023b0e342e82bd643e881adf83a693d3f9f2344681718d0883be9db",
      "skos:note": "A determination under this section is a disallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12a-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12A(6) Determination of primary universal service providers",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(6) A determination under this section is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nNote:\nA determination that the Minister is taken to have made under this\nsection because of section 12D or 12E is not a disallowable instrument\n(see subsections 12D(2) and 12E(6)).\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            25"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a-ss-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a-ss-6"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a-ss-6-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits a determination from being a disallowable instrument.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12a-ss-6-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permits a determination to be made under this section.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12B Effect of determination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A determination under section 12A takes effect on the day\nspecified in the determination. That day must not be before the day\non which notice of the determination is published in the Gazette.\n\n(2) If such a determination is expressed to cease to have effect at a\nspecified time, the determination ceases to have effect at that time.\n\n(3) A variation or revocation of a determination under section 12A\ntakes effect on the day specified for the purpose in the instrument\nof variation or revocation. That day must not be before notice of\nthe instrument is published in the Gazette.\n\n(4) If the Minister revokes a determination under section 12A, the\nMinister may determine in writing arrangements to deal with any\nissues of a transitional nature that may arise as a result of the\nrevocation.\n\n(5) A copy of a determination under subsection (4) must be published\nin the Gazette.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A determination under section 12A takes effect on the day\nspecified in the determination. That day must not be before the day\non which notice of the determination is published in the Gazette.\n\n(2) If such a determination is expressed to cease to have effect at a\nspecified time, the determination ceases to have effect at that time.\n\n(3) A variation or revocation of a determination under section 12A\ntakes effect on the day specified for the purpose in the instrument\nof variation or revocation. That day must not be before notice of\nthe instrument is published in the Gazette.\n\n(4) If the Minister revokes a determination under section 12A, the\nMinister may determine in writing arrangements to deal with any\nissues of a transitional nature that may arise as a result of the\nrevocation.\n\n(5) A copy of a determination under subsection (4) must be published\nin the Gazette.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12b-ss-1"
        },
        {
