    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-26"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\nby supplying alternative telecommunications services in\naccordance with an approved ATS marketing plan, is taken to have\nfulfilled any other obligation that arises under this Act because of\nthat service obligation to the extent that the other obligation applies\nto the supply of alternative telecommunications services.\n\n(2) The ACA may determine in writing requirements that a primary\nuniversal service provider must comply with if the provider intends\nto cease supplying alternative telecommunications services in\naccordance with an approved ATS marketing plan. A copy of the\ndetermination must be given to the provider.\n\n(3) The provider must comply with those requirements (as well as any\nrequirements in the plan).",
      "skos:definition": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\nby supplying alternative telecommunications services in\naccordance with an approved ATS marketing plan, is taken to have\nfulfilled any other obligation that arises under this Act because of\nthat service obligation to the extent that the other obligation applies\nto the supply of alternative telecommunications services.\n\n(2) The ACA may determine in writing requirements that a primary\nuniversal service provider must comply with if the provider intends\nto cease supplying alternative telecommunications services in\naccordance with an approved ATS marketing plan. A copy of the\ndetermination must be given to the provider.\n\n(3) The provider must comply with those requirements (as well as any\nrequirements in the plan).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a60311de45972967fc08da7a0dae04b6d4f030f2d1259eb48aede211bdcd00bd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-26",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\nby supplying alternative telecommunications services in\naccordance with an approved ATS marketing plan, is taken to have\nfulfilled any other obligation that arises under this Act because of\nthat service obligation to the extent that the other obligation applies\nto the supply of alternative telecommunications services.\n\n(2) The ACA may determine in writing requirements that a primary\nuniversal service provider must comply with if the provider intends\nto cease supplying alternative telecommunications services in\naccordance with an approved ATS marketing plan. A copy of the\ndetermination must be given to the provider.\n\n(3) The provider must comply with those requirements (as well as any\nrequirements in the plan)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
