    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12d-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12D(2) Transitional: when Telstra is taken to be a primary universal",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Despite subsection 12A(6), the determination that the Minister is\ntaken to have made is not a disallowable instrument for the\npurposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nInstead, a notice must be published in the Gazette to the effect that\nTelstra is the primary universal service provider for the area in\nrespect of that service obligation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12d-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
