    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12E Effect of certain agreements under the Telstra Corporation Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to agreements under section 56 or 57 of the\nTelstra Corporation Act 1991 made between the Commonwealth\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            27\nand a person (including a State or Territory) that are expressed to\nalso have effect for the purposes of:\n\n(a) this subsection; or\n\n(b) subsection 20(2B) of this Act as in force immediately before\nthe commencement of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications\n(Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment\nAct (No. 2) 2000.\n\n(2) The Minister is taken to have properly made:\n\n(a) a determination under section 9G that each of the areas,\nspecified in the agreement as a universal service area in\nrespect of a service obligation, is a universal service area in\nrespect of that service obligation for the purposes of this Act;\nand\n\n(b) a determination under section 12A that the person is a\nprimary universal service provider for each of the areas, in\nrespect of the service obligation or obligations, specified in\nthe agreement.\nThose determinations are referred to in this section as deemed\ndeterminations.\n\n(3) The deemed determinations take effect as follows:\n\n(a) if the commencement date (see subsection (4)) is the same\nfor each of the areas—they take effect on that\ncommencement date; or\n\n(b) if there are different commencement dates for different\nareas—they take effect for those different areas on those\ndifferent dates.\n\n(4) The commencement date or dates for an area is or are as follows:\n\n(a) if the agreement specifies a single date as the commencement\ndate for the area—subject to paragraph (c), the\ncommencement date for the area is the specified date;\n\n(b) if the agreement specifies different dates as the\ncommencement dates for different areas—subject to\nparagraph (c), the commencement dates for those areas are\nthe specified dates;\n\n(c) if a determination under subsection (5) specifies a date as the\ncommencement date for the area or areas—the\ncommencement date for the area or areas is the specified date\n(regardless of any dates specified in the agreement).\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to agreements under section 56 or 57 of the\nTelstra Corporation Act 1991 made between the Commonwealth\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            27\nand a person (including a State or Territory) that are expressed to\nalso have effect for the purposes of:\n\n(a) this subsection; or\n\n(b) subsection 20(2B) of this Act as in force immediately before\nthe commencement of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications\n(Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment\nAct (No. 2) 2000.\n\n(2) The Minister is taken to have properly made:\n\n(a) a determination under section 9G that each of the areas,\nspecified in the agreement as a universal service area in\nrespect of a service obligation, is a universal service area in\nrespect of that service obligation for the purposes of this Act;\nand\n\n(b) a determination under section 12A that the person is a\nprimary universal service provider for each of the areas, in\nrespect of the service obligation or obligations, specified in\nthe agreement.\nThose determinations are referred to in this section as deemed\ndeterminations.\n\n(3) The deemed determinations take effect as follows:\n\n(a) if the commencement date (see subsection (4)) is the same\nfor each of the areas—they take effect on that\ncommencement date; or\n\n(b) if there are different commencement dates for different\nareas—they take effect for those different areas on those\ndifferent dates.\n\n(4) The commencement date or dates for an area is or are as follows:\n\n(a) if the agreement specifies a single date as the commencement\ndate for the area—subject to paragraph (c), the\ncommencement date for the area is the specified date;\n\n(b) if the agreement specifies different dates as the\ncommencement dates for different areas—subject to\nparagraph (c), the commencement dates for those areas are\nthe specified dates",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12e-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12e-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12e-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c73738ee7cd7df0e1fa2b67103ac1d67f07529035b1a4528ea05926fb794874e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12E Effect of certain agreements under the Telstra Corporation Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to agreements under section 56 or 57 of the\nTelstra Corporation Act 1991 made between the Commonwealth\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            27\nand a person (including a State or Territory) that are expressed to\nalso have effect for the purposes of:\n\n(a) this subsection; or\n\n(b) subsection 20(2B) of this Act as in force immediately before\nthe commencement of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications\n(Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment\nAct (No. 2) 2000.\n\n(2) The Minister is taken to have properly made:\n\n(a) a determination under section 9G that each of the areas,\nspecified in the agreement as a universal service area in\nrespect of a service obligation, is a universal service area in\nrespect of that service obligation for the purposes of this Act;\nand\n\n(b) a determination under section 12A that the person is a\nprimary universal service provider for each of the areas, in\nrespect of the service obligation or obligations, specified in\nthe agreement.\nThose determinations are referred to in this section as deemed\ndeterminations.\n\n(3) The deemed determinations take effect as follows:\n\n(a) if the commencement date (see subsection (4)) is the same\nfor each of the areas—they take effect on that\ncommencement date; or\n\n(b) if there are different commencement dates for different\nareas—they take effect for those different areas on those\ndifferent dates.\n\n(4) The commencement date or dates for an area is or are as follows:\n\n(a) if the agreement specifies a single date as the commencement\ndate for the area—subject to paragraph (c), the\ncommencement date for the area is the specified date;\n\n(b) if the agreement specifies different dates as the\ncommencement dates for different areas—subject to\nparagraph (c), the commencement dates for those areas are\nthe specified dates;\n\n(c) if a determination under subsection (5) specifies a date as the\ncommencement date for the area or areas—the\ncommencement date for the area or areas is the specified date\n(regardless of any dates specified in the agreement).\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
    },
