      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "...if there are different commencement dates..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12e-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12E(4) Effect of certain agreements under the Telstra Corporation Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12e-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The commencement date or dates for an area is or are as follows:\n\n(a) if the agreement specifies a single date as the commencement\ndate for the area—subject to paragraph (c), the\ncommencement date for the area is the specified date;\n\n(b) if the agreement specifies different dates as the\ncommencement dates for different areas—subject to\nparagraph (c), the commencement dates for those areas are\nthe specified dates;\n\n(c) if a determination under subsection (5) specifies a date as the\ncommencement date for the area or areas—the\ncommencement date for the area or areas is the specified date\n(regardless of any dates specified in the agreement).\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The commencement date or dates for an area is or are as follows:\n\n(a) if the agreement specifies a single date as the commencement\ndate for the area—subject to paragraph (c), the\ncommencement date for the area is the specified date;\n\n(b) if the agreement specifies different dates as the\ncommencement dates for different areas—subject to\nparagraph (c), the commencement dates for those areas are\nthe specified dates;\n\n(c) if a determination under subsection (5) specifies a date as the\ncommencement date for the area or areas—the\ncommencement date for the area or areas is the specified date\n(regardless of any dates specified in the agreement).\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12e"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12e-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c5abac20504af5bcc18d277edd7028d03eda7b756dea1cc968ec2a520a04fd43",
      "skos:note": "Defines commencement dates for areas under the agreement"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12e-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12E(4) Effect of certain agreements under the Telstra Corporation Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The commencement date or dates for an area is or are as follows:\n\n(a) if the agreement specifies a single date as the commencement\ndate for the area—subject to paragraph (c), the\ncommencement date for the area is the specified date;\n\n(b) if the agreement specifies different dates as the\ncommencement dates for different areas—subject to\nparagraph (c), the commencement dates for those areas are\nthe specified dates;\n\n(c) if a determination under subsection (5) specifies a date as the\ncommencement date for the area or areas—the\ncommencement date for the area or areas is the specified date\n(regardless of any dates specified in the agreement).\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12e-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12e-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-28",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-28"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\nA commencement date cannot be a date before the agreement is\nmade, or before the commencement of this subsection or the\nsubsection referred to in paragraph (1)(a).\n\n(5) The Minister may make a written determination specifying a date\nas the commencement date for the area or areas specified in the\nagreement as universal service areas. A copy of the determination\nmust be published in the Gazette.\n\n(6) Despite subsections 9G(5) and 12A(6), the deemed determinations\nare not disallowable instruments for the purposes of section 46A of\nthe Acts Interpretation Act 1901. Instead, a notice must be\npublished in the Gazette that:\n\n(a) states that the person is a primary universal service provider\nfor the area or areas concerned, in respect of the service\nobligation or obligations concerned; and\n\n(b) includes the relevant commencement date or dates.\n\n(7) However, a variation or revocation of a deemed determination is a\ndisallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n(8) This section applies to an agreement whether made before, on or\nafter the commencement of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications\n(Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act\n(No. 2) 2000.",
      "skos:definition": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\nA commencement date cannot be a date before the agreement is\nmade, or before the commencement of this subsection or the\nsubsection referred to in paragraph (1)(a).\n\n(5) The Minister may make a written determination specifying a date\nas the commencement date for the area or areas specified in the\nagreement as universal service areas. A copy of the determination\nmust be published in the Gazette.\n\n(6) Despite subsections 9G(5) and 12A(6), the deemed determinations\nare not disallowable instruments for the purposes of section 46A of\nthe Acts Interpretation Act 1901. Instead, a notice must be\npublished in the Gazette that:\n\n(a) states that the person is a primary universal service provider\nfor the area or areas concerned, in respect of the service\nobligation or obligations concerned; and\n\n(b) includes the relevant commencement date or dates.\n\n(7) However, a variation or revocation of a deemed determination is a\ndisallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n(8) This section applies to an agreement whether made before, on or\nafter the commencement of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications\n(Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act\n(No. 2) 2000.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-28-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-28-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-28-ss-7"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-28-ss-8"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "85a9ab57ab2c85815d6aac50233eb43c1cbb5802ea6d2caadf9e70d41de82dc9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-28",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\nA commencement date cannot be a date before the agreement is\nmade, or before the commencement of this subsection or the\nsubsection referred to in paragraph (1)(a).\n\n(5) The Minister may make a written determination specifying a date\nas the commencement date for the area or areas specified in the\nagreement as universal service areas. A copy of the determination\nmust be published in the Gazette.\n\n(6) Despite subsections 9G(5) and 12A(6), the deemed determinations\nare not disallowable instruments for the purposes of section 46A of\nthe Acts Interpretation Act 1901. Instead, a notice must be\npublished in the Gazette that:\n\n(a) states that the person is a primary universal service provider\nfor the area or areas concerned, in respect of the service\nobligation or obligations concerned; and\n\n(b) includes the relevant commencement date or dates.\n\n(7) However, a variation or revocation of a deemed determination is a\ndisallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n(8) This section applies to an agreement whether made before, on or\nafter the commencement of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications\n(Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act\n(No. 2) 2000."
    },
