    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-28-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28(6) Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-28-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "(6) Despite subsections 9G(5) and 12A(6), the deemed determinations\nare not disallowable instruments for the purposes of section 46A of\nthe Acts Interpretation Act 1901. Instead, a notice must be\npublished in the Gazette that:\n\n(a) states that the person is a primary universal service provider\nfor the area or areas concerned, in respect of the service\nobligation or obligations concerned; and\n\n(b) includes the relevant commencement date or dates.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) Despite subsections 9G(5) and 12A(6), the deemed determinations\nare not disallowable instruments for the purposes of section 46A of\nthe Acts Interpretation Act 1901. Instead, a notice must be\npublished in the Gazette that:\n\n(a) states that the person is a primary universal service provider\nfor the area or areas concerned, in respect of the service\nobligation or obligations concerned; and\n\n(b) includes the relevant commencement date or dates.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-28"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-28-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-28-ss-6-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-28-ss-6-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "43f9cba15d162e4e9f40d4d6418eeb0dfc9d72391be35fddd11c39c5ba8bcc30",
      "skos:note": "Notice must be published in the Gazette stating a person is a primary universal service provider.",
      "dc:description": "Notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-28-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28(6) Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "(6) Despite subsections 9G(5) and 12A(6), the deemed determinations\nare not disallowable instruments for the purposes of section 46A of\nthe Acts Interpretation Act 1901. Instead, a notice must be\npublished in the Gazette that:\n\n(a) states that the person is a primary universal service provider\nfor the area or areas concerned, in respect of the service\nobligation or obligations concerned; and\n\n(b) includes the relevant commencement date or dates."
    },
