    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12ea",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12EA Exclusive access to universal service subsidy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12ea"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person is a primary universal service provider for a universal\nservice area in respect of a service obligation because of subsection\n12E(2):\n\n(a) the Minister must not determine any other person to be a\nprimary universal service provider; and\n\n(b) the ACA must not approve any other person as a competing\nuniversal service provider;\nfor that area in respect of that service obligation.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies while the agreement referred to in\nsubsection 12E(2) remains in force in relation to that area but no\nlonger than 3 years after the commencement date for the area.\n\n(3) This section applies despite anything else in this Part.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            29\nSubdivision C—Policy statements and standard marketing\nplans of primary universal service providers",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a person is a primary universal service provider for a universal\nservice area in respect of a service obligation because of subsection\n12E(2):\n\n(a) the Minister must not determine any other person to be a\nprimary universal service provider; and\n\n(b) the ACA must not approve any other person as a competing\nuniversal service provider;\nfor that area in respect of that service obligation.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies while the agreement referred to in\nsubsection 12E(2) remains in force in relation to that area but no\nlonger than 3 years after the commencement date for the area.\n\n(3) This section applies despite anything else in this Part.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            29\nSubdivision C—Policy statements and standard marketing\nplans of primary universal service providers",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12ea-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12ea-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12ea-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d44b12c3886ab14304f2701ab58bd21533fc1a00a39e8b4f32f4a24f817b2c56"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12ea",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12EA Exclusive access to universal service subsidy",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person is a primary universal service provider for a universal\nservice area in respect of a service obligation because of subsection\n12E(2):\n\n(a) the Minister must not determine any other person to be a\nprimary universal service provider; and\n\n(b) the ACA must not approve any other person as a competing\nuniversal service provider;\nfor that area in respect of that service obligation.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies while the agreement referred to in\nsubsection 12E(2) remains in force in relation to that area but no\nlonger than 3 years after the commencement date for the area.\n\n(3) This section applies despite anything else in this Part.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            29\nSubdivision C—Policy statements and standard marketing\nplans of primary universal service providers"
    },
