    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12F Meaning of expressions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A draft policy statement for a primary universal service provider is\na general statement of the policy the provider will apply in\nsupplying equipment, goods or services as a primary universal\nservice provider.\n\n(2) A draft policy statement that has been approved by the ACA under\nsection 12K, and that is in force, is an approved policy statement\nfor the primary universal service provider concerned.\n\n(3) A draft standard marketing plan for a primary universal service\nprovider for a universal service area in respect of a service\nobligation is a plan that sets out:\n\n(a) the equipment, goods or services that the provider will supply\nin fulfilment of that service obligation, so far as it relates to\nthat area; and\n\n(b) the arrangements for supplying and marketing the equipment,\ngoods or services;\nbut does not deal with alternative telecommunications services.\n\n(4) A draft standard marketing plan that has been approved by the\nACA under section 12K, and that is in force, is an approved\nstandard marketing plan for the primary universal service\nprovider concerned.\n\n(5) A draft or approved standard marketing plan may cover one or\nmore universal service areas in respect of one or more service\nobligations.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A draft policy statement for a primary universal service provider is\na general statement of the policy the provider will apply in\nsupplying equipment, goods or services as a primary universal\nservice provider.\n\n(2) A draft policy statement that has been approved by the ACA under\nsection 12K, and that is in force, is an approved policy statement\nfor the primary universal service provider concerned.\n\n(3) A draft standard marketing plan for a primary universal service\nprovider for a universal service area in respect of a service\nobligation is a plan that sets out:\n\n(a) the equipment, goods or services that the provider will supply\nin fulfilment of that service obligation, so far as it relates to\nthat area; and\n\n(b) the arrangements for supplying and marketing the equipment,\ngoods or services;\nbut does not deal with alternative telecommunications services.\n\n(4) A draft standard marketing plan that has been approved by the\nACA under section 12K, and that is in force, is an approved\nstandard marketing plan for the primary universal service\nprovider concerned.\n\n(5) A draft or approved standard marketing plan may cover one or\nmore universal service areas in respect of one or more service\nobligations.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12f-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12f-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12f-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6a646fa3c28aa5f7a0130379a08bc659f5eace619387c2c4e5cb349feaab4d33"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12F Meaning of expressions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A draft policy statement for a primary universal service provider is\na general statement of the policy the provider will apply in\nsupplying equipment, goods or services as a primary universal\nservice provider.\n\n(2) A draft policy statement that has been approved by the ACA under\nsection 12K, and that is in force, is an approved policy statement\nfor the primary universal service provider concerned.\n\n(3) A draft standard marketing plan for a primary universal service\nprovider for a universal service area in respect of a service\nobligation is a plan that sets out:\n\n(a) the equipment, goods or services that the provider will supply\nin fulfilment of that service obligation, so far as it relates to\nthat area; and\n\n(b) the arrangements for supplying and marketing the equipment,\ngoods or services;\nbut does not deal with alternative telecommunications services.\n\n(4) A draft standard marketing plan that has been approved by the\nACA under section 12K, and that is in force, is an approved\nstandard marketing plan for the primary universal service\nprovider concerned.\n\n(5) A draft or approved standard marketing plan may cover one or\nmore universal service areas in respect of one or more service\nobligations."
    },
