      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "50e1d80ab677d249e178dfaed4b70d70dbf43e72ccc245e1ca4ff417e5712f80",
      "skos:note": "Draft standard marketing plan for a primary universal service provider must set out equipment, goods or services to be supplied and arrangements for supplying and marketing."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12f-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12F(3) Meaning of expressions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "(3) A draft standard marketing plan for a primary universal service\nprovider for a universal service area in respect of a service\nobligation is a plan that sets out:\n\n(a) the equipment, goods or services that the provider will supply\nin fulfilment of that service obligation, so far as it relates to\nthat area; and\n\n(b) the arrangements for supplying and marketing the equipment,\ngoods or services;\nbut does not deal with alternative telecommunications services."
    },
