    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12H Obligation to submit a draft policy statement and draft",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "standard marketing plan\n\nWithin 90 days after a person becomes a primary universal service\nprovider for a universal service area in respect of a service\nobligation, the provider must give the ACA:\n\n(a) a draft policy statement, or draft variation of an approved\npolicy statement; and\n\n(b) a draft standard marketing plan, or draft variation of an\napproved standard marketing plan;\ncovering that area in respect of that service obligation.",
      "skos:definition": "standard marketing plan\n\nWithin 90 days after a person becomes a primary universal service\nprovider for a universal service area in respect of a service\nobligation, the provider must give the ACA:\n\n(a) a draft policy statement, or draft variation of an approved\npolicy statement; and\n\n(b) a draft standard marketing plan, or draft variation of an\napproved standard marketing plan;\ncovering that area in respect of that service obligation.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12h-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12h-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "65d2ea2bbe955bcb6c96651648d7c5b8f76d5e659bc14106917b21d18a397751",
      "skos:note": "Primary universal service provider must submit draft policy statement and standard marketing plan within 90 days.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12H Obligation to submit a draft policy statement and draft",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "standard marketing plan\n\nWithin 90 days after a person becomes a primary universal service\nprovider for a universal service area in respect of a service\nobligation, the provider must give the ACA:\n\n(a) a draft policy statement, or draft variation of an approved\npolicy statement; and\n\n(b) a draft standard marketing plan, or draft variation of an\napproved standard marketing plan;\ncovering that area in respect of that service obligation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12h-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12h"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12h-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12J Public consultation required on draft policy statement and draft",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "standard marketing plan\n\n(1) Before giving the ACA a draft policy statement or draft standard\nmarketing plan, a primary universal service provider must:\n\n(a) publish a preliminary version of the draft and invite members\nof the public to make submissions to the provider about the\npreliminary version within a specified period (which must be\nat least 30 days); and\n\n(b) give consideration to any submissions received from\nmembers of the public within that period.\n\n(2) When giving the draft to the ACA, the provider must include\nadvice on the submissions considered and any changes made to the\ndraft as a result.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            31\n\n(3) However, this section does not apply to a fresh draft policy\nstatement, or fresh draft standard marketing plan, given to the ACA\nby a primary universal service provider in accordance with a\ndirection under paragraph 12M(2)(b) unless the ACA notifies the\nprovider in writing that it does apply to the document.",
      "skos:definition": "standard marketing plan\n\n(1) Before giving the ACA a draft policy statement or draft standard\nmarketing plan, a primary universal service provider must:\n\n(a) publish a preliminary version of the draft and invite members\nof the public to make submissions to the provider about the\npreliminary version within a specified period (which must be\nat least 30 days); and\n\n(b) give consideration to any submissions received from\nmembers of the public within that period.\n\n(2) When giving the draft to the ACA, the provider must include\nadvice on the submissions considered and any changes made to the\ndraft as a result.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            31\n\n(3) However, this section does not apply to a fresh draft policy\nstatement, or fresh draft standard marketing plan, given to the ACA\nby a primary universal service provider in accordance with a\ndirection under paragraph 12M(2)(b) unless the ACA notifies the\nprovider in writing that it does apply to the document.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12j-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12j-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ed7fcf8c880a53dd94a2f926f51c76e36d3a53f6552903555770e0a4dab29516"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12J Public consultation required on draft policy statement and draft",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "standard marketing plan\n\n(1) Before giving the ACA a draft policy statement or draft standard\nmarketing plan, a primary universal service provider must:\n\n(a) publish a preliminary version of the draft and invite members\nof the public to make submissions to the provider about the\npreliminary version within a specified period (which must be\nat least 30 days); and\n\n(b) give consideration to any submissions received from\nmembers of the public within that period.\n\n(2) When giving the draft to the ACA, the provider must include\nadvice on the submissions considered and any changes made to the\ndraft as a result.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            31\n\n(3) However, this section does not apply to a fresh draft policy\nstatement, or fresh draft standard marketing plan, given to the ACA\nby a primary universal service provider in accordance with a\ndirection under paragraph 12M(2)(b) unless the ACA notifies the\nprovider in writing that it does apply to the document."
    },
