    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12L Approval of draft standard marketing plan",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACA must approve, or refuse to approve, a draft standard\nmarketing plan that a primary universal service provider gives to\nthe ACA.\n\n(2) The ACA must not approve the draft unless it is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the draft specifies appropriate equipment, goods or services\nthat the provider will supply in fulfilment of the service\nobligation concerned, so far as it relates to the universal\nservice area concerned; and\n\n(b) the draft adequately deals with how the provider will fulfil\nthat service obligation, so far as it relates to that area; and\n\n(c) the draft sets out appropriate terms and conditions on which\nthe equipment, goods or services are to be supplied; and\n\n(d) the draft sets out appropriate arrangements for the marketing\nof the supply of the equipment, goods or services to persons\nin the universal service area concerned.\n\n(3) In deciding whether to approve the draft, the ACA must also have\nregard to:\n\n(a) whether the draft complies with the requirements (if any)\nunder section 12G; and\n\n(b) any other matters determined in writing by the Minister for\nthe purposes of this paragraph; and\n\n(c) any other matters the ACA considers relevant.\n\n(4) A copy of a determination made for the purposes of\nparagraph (3)(b) must be published in the Gazette.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACA must approve, or refuse to approve, a draft standard\nmarketing plan that a primary universal service provider gives to\nthe ACA.\n\n(2) The ACA must not approve the draft unless it is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the draft specifies appropriate equipment, goods or services\nthat the provider will supply in fulfilment of the service\nobligation concerned, so far as it relates to the universal\nservice area concerned; and\n\n(b) the draft adequately deals with how the provider will fulfil\nthat service obligation, so far as it relates to that area; and\n\n(c) the draft sets out appropriate terms and conditions on which\nthe equipment, goods or services are to be supplied; and\n\n(d) the draft sets out appropriate arrangements for the marketing\nof the supply of the equipment, goods or services to persons\nin the universal service area concerned.\n\n(3) In deciding whether to approve the draft, the ACA must also have\nregard to:\n\n(a) whether the draft complies with the requirements (if any)\nunder section 12G; and\n\n(b) any other matters determined in writing by the Minister for\nthe purposes of this paragraph; and\n\n(c) any other matters the ACA considers relevant.\n\n(4) A copy of a determination made for the purposes of\nparagraph (3)(b) must be published in the Gazette.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12l-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12l-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12l-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12l-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c2101bc57096d45cdac98a4b39171bcaebbca3470343d41ad078427b479db185"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12l",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12L Approval of draft standard marketing plan",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACA must approve, or refuse to approve, a draft standard\nmarketing plan that a primary universal service provider gives to\nthe ACA.\n\n(2) The ACA must not approve the draft unless it is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the draft specifies appropriate equipment, goods or services\nthat the provider will supply in fulfilment of the service\nobligation concerned, so far as it relates to the universal\nservice area concerned; and\n\n(b) the draft adequately deals with how the provider will fulfil\nthat service obligation, so far as it relates to that area; and\n\n(c) the draft sets out appropriate terms and conditions on which\nthe equipment, goods or services are to be supplied; and\n\n(d) the draft sets out appropriate arrangements for the marketing\nof the supply of the equipment, goods or services to persons\nin the universal service area concerned.\n\n(3) In deciding whether to approve the draft, the ACA must also have\nregard to:\n\n(a) whether the draft complies with the requirements (if any)\nunder section 12G; and\n\n(b) any other matters determined in writing by the Minister for\nthe purposes of this paragraph; and\n\n(c) any other matters the ACA considers relevant.\n\n(4) A copy of a determination made for the purposes of\nparagraph (3)(b) must be published in the Gazette."
    },
