    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12M Notice of decision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACA must give written notice of the ACA’s decision whether\nto approve a draft policy statement, or draft standard marketing\nplan, to the primary universal service provider concerned.\n\n(2) If the ACA refuses to approve the draft, the ACA:\n\n(a) must give the provider written notice of the reasons for that\nrefusal; and\n\n(b) may, by giving written notice to the provider, direct the\nprovider to give the ACA, within a specified period and in\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            33\nspecified terms, a fresh draft policy statement or fresh draft\nstandard marketing plan as the case may be.\n\n(3) The provider must comply with a direction under paragraph (2)(b).\n\n(4) A copy of the notice under subsection (1) must be published in the\nGazette if the decision is to approve the draft.\nSubdivision D—ATS marketing plans of primary universal\nservice providers",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACA must give written notice of the ACA’s decision whether\nto approve a draft policy statement, or draft standard marketing\nplan, to the primary universal service provider concerned.\n\n(2) If the ACA refuses to approve the draft, the ACA:\n\n(a) must give the provider written notice of the reasons for that\nrefusal; and\n\n(b) may, by giving written notice to the provider, direct the\nprovider to give the ACA, within a specified period and in\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            33\nspecified terms, a fresh draft policy statement or fresh draft\nstandard marketing plan as the case may be.\n\n(3) The provider must comply with a direction under paragraph (2)(b).\n\n(4) A copy of the notice under subsection (1) must be published in the\nGazette if the decision is to approve the draft.\nSubdivision D—ATS marketing plans of primary universal\nservice providers",
      "cml:hasPart": [
