      "cml:logicSummary": "Regulates timeframes for supply of equipment, goods or services.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12r",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12R Primary universal service provider may submit a draft ATS",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12r"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "marketing plan\n\n(1) A primary universal service provider for a universal service\nobligation in respect of a service obligation, who wishes to supply\nalternative telecommunications services in fulfilment of that\nservice obligation so far as it relates to that area, may give to the\nACA a draft ATS marketing plan covering the supply of those\nservices.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, the primary universal service provider is still\nrequired to fulfil that service obligation so far as it relates to that\narea in accordance with section 9.",
      "skos:definition": "marketing plan\n\n(1) A primary universal service provider for a universal service\nobligation in respect of a service obligation, who wishes to supply\nalternative telecommunications services in fulfilment of that\nservice obligation so far as it relates to that area, may give to the\nACA a draft ATS marketing plan covering the supply of those\nservices.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, the primary universal service provider is still\nrequired to fulfil that service obligation so far as it relates to that\narea in accordance with section 9.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12r-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12r-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f53de70e2a95b054bddd1ae8cc09a004379bb01b2bbe1100c42e6f8bcd25d04c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12r",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12R Primary universal service provider may submit a draft ATS",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "marketing plan\n\n(1) A primary universal service provider for a universal service\nobligation in respect of a service obligation, who wishes to supply\nalternative telecommunications services in fulfilment of that\nservice obligation so far as it relates to that area, may give to the\nACA a draft ATS marketing plan covering the supply of those\nservices.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, the primary universal service provider is still\nrequired to fulfil that service obligation so far as it relates to that\narea in accordance with section 9."
    },
