    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12s",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12S Public consultation required on draft ATS marketing plan",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12s"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before deciding whether to approve a draft ATS marketing plan,\nthe ACA must require the provider concerned:\n\n(a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft and invite\nmembers of the public to make submissions to the applicant\nabout the preliminary version within a specified period\n(which must be at least 30 days); and\n\n(b) to give consideration to any submissions received from\nmembers of the public within that period; and\n\n(c) to advise the ACA on those submissions and any changes\nmade to the draft as a result.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            35\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies only if a draft ATS marketing plan is\nmaterially different from an ATS marketing plan previously\napproved by the ACA.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Before deciding whether to approve a draft ATS marketing plan,\nthe ACA must require the provider concerned:\n\n(a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft and invite\nmembers of the public to make submissions to the applicant\nabout the preliminary version within a specified period\n(which must be at least 30 days); and\n\n(b) to give consideration to any submissions received from\nmembers of the public within that period; and\n\n(c) to advise the ACA on those submissions and any changes\nmade to the draft as a result.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            35\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies only if a draft ATS marketing plan is\nmaterially different from an ATS marketing plan previously\napproved by the ACA.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12s-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12s-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6c565b8bd3eb8d79c5c8a8614802f7308cb9c44c0f1366863aa10ae8a0ce659b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12s",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12S Public consultation required on draft ATS marketing plan",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before deciding whether to approve a draft ATS marketing plan,\nthe ACA must require the provider concerned:\n\n(a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft and invite\nmembers of the public to make submissions to the applicant\nabout the preliminary version within a specified period\n(which must be at least 30 days); and\n\n(b) to give consideration to any submissions received from\nmembers of the public within that period; and\n\n(c) to advise the ACA on those submissions and any changes\nmade to the draft as a result.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            35\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies only if a draft ATS marketing plan is\nmaterially different from an ATS marketing plan previously\napproved by the ACA."
    },
