        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5a47324bdc2af33891a313d4209c26c51140a4a7c70a95445705f71e2f1b19ae"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-36",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 40,
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\ntelecommunications services in fulfilment of that service\nobligation, so far as it relates to that area; and\n\n(g) the requirements of section 12S have been met.\n\n(3) The procedures referred to in paragraph (2)(f) must include the\ngiving of at least 45 days’ notice to the ACA, or such other notice\nas the ACA determines in writing is adequate for the purposes of\nthat paragraph.\n\n(4) In deciding whether to approve the draft, the ACA must also have\nregard to:\n\n(a) whether the draft complies with the requirements (if any)\nunder section 12Q; and\n\n(b) any other matters determined in writing by the Minister for\nthe purposes of this paragraph; and\n\n(c) any other matters the ACA considers relevant.\n\n(5) A copy of a determination made for the purposes of\nparagraph (2)(f) or (4)(b) must be published in the Gazette."
    },
