    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12w",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12W Variation of approved policy statement, approved standard",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12w"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "marketing plan or approved ATS marketing plan\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an approved policy statement for a primary universal service\nprovider (the current statement) is in force; or\n\n(b) an approved standard marketing plan for a primary universal\nservice provider (the current plan) is in force; or\n\n(c) an approved ATS marketing plan for a primary universal\nservice provider (the current plan) is in force;\nand the provider gives the ACA a draft variation of the current\nstatement or current plan.\n\n(2) The ACA must:\n\n(a) approve the variation; or\n\n(b) refuse to approve the variation.\n\n(3) Before deciding whether to approve the variation, the ACA may, if\nthe ACA considers it appropriate, require the provider:\n\n(a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft variation and\ninvite members of the public to make submissions to the\nprovider about the preliminary version within a specified\nperiod; and\n\n(b) to give consideration to any submissions from members of\nthe public received within that period; and\n\n(c) to advise the ACA on those submissions and any changes\nmade to the draft variation as a result.\n\n(4) The ACA must not approve the variation unless it is satisfied that:\n\n(a) in the case of a draft variation of an approved policy\nstatement—if the provider were to give the ACA a draft\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "marketing plan or approved ATS marketing plan\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an approved policy statement for a primary universal service\nprovider (the current statement) is in force; or\n\n(b) an approved standard marketing plan for a primary universal\nservice provider (the current plan) is in force; or\n\n(c) an approved ATS marketing plan for a primary universal\nservice provider (the current plan) is in force;\nand the provider gives the ACA a draft variation of the current\nstatement or current plan.\n\n(2) The ACA must:\n\n(a) approve the variation; or\n\n(b) refuse to approve the variation.\n\n(3) Before deciding whether to approve the variation, the ACA may, if\nthe ACA considers it appropriate, require the provider:\n\n(a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft variation and\ninvite members of the public to make submissions to the\nprovider about the preliminary version within a specified\nperiod; and\n\n(b) to give consideration to any submissions from members of\nthe public received within that period; and\n\n(c) to advise the ACA on those submissions and any changes\nmade to the draft variation as a result.\n\n(4) The ACA must not approve the variation unless it is satisfied that:\n\n(a) in the case of a draft variation of an approved policy\nstatement—if the provider were to give the ACA a draft\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "cml:hasPart": [
