    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12y",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12Y Minister may direct variation or replacement of policy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12y"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.42",
      "values:originalText": "statement or standard marketing plan\n\n(1) If an approved policy statement for a primary universal service\nprovider is in force, the Minister may give the provider a written\nnotice requiring the provider:\n\n(a) within a specified period and in specified terms, to give the\nACA a draft variation of the statement; or\n\n(b) within a specified period and in specified terms, to give the\nACA a fresh draft policy statement that is expressed to\nreplace the statement.\n\n(2) If an approved standard marketing plan for a primary universal\nservice provider is in force, the Minister may give the provider a\nwritten notice requiring the provider:\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            39\n\n(a) within a specified period and in specified terms, to give the\nACA a draft variation of the plan; or\n\n(b) within a specified period and in specified terms, to give the\nACA a fresh draft standard marketing plan that is expressed\nto replace the plan.\n\n(3) A primary universal provider to whom a notice under this section\nis given must comply with the notice.",
      "skos:definition": "statement or standard marketing plan\n\n(1) If an approved policy statement for a primary universal service\nprovider is in force, the Minister may give the provider a written\nnotice requiring the provider:\n\n(a) within a specified period and in specified terms, to give the\nACA a draft variation of the statement; or\n\n(b) within a specified period and in specified terms, to give the\nACA a fresh draft policy statement that is expressed to\nreplace the statement.\n\n(2) If an approved standard marketing plan for a primary universal\nservice provider is in force, the Minister may give the provider a\nwritten notice requiring the provider:\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            39\n\n(a) within a specified period and in specified terms, to give the\nACA a draft variation of the plan; or\n\n(b) within a specified period and in specified terms, to give the\nACA a fresh draft standard marketing plan that is expressed\nto replace the plan.\n\n(3) A primary universal provider to whom a notice under this section\nis given must comply with the notice.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12y-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12y-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12y-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eccb75fb94e0d0ddda35b8eadc9819bdcab87a4bbf00324588e2b9a4130ef3f7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12y",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12Y Minister may direct variation or replacement of policy",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 42,
      "values:originalText": "statement or standard marketing plan\n\n(1) If an approved policy statement for a primary universal service\nprovider is in force, the Minister may give the provider a written\nnotice requiring the provider:\n\n(a) within a specified period and in specified terms, to give the\nACA a draft variation of the statement; or\n\n(b) within a specified period and in specified terms, to give the\nACA a fresh draft policy statement that is expressed to\nreplace the statement.\n\n(2) If an approved standard marketing plan for a primary universal\nservice provider is in force, the Minister may give the provider a\nwritten notice requiring the provider:\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            39\n\n(a) within a specified period and in specified terms, to give the\nACA a draft variation of the plan; or\n\n(b) within a specified period and in specified terms, to give the\nACA a fresh draft standard marketing plan that is expressed\nto replace the plan.\n\n(3) A primary universal provider to whom a notice under this section\nis given must comply with the notice."
    },
