    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12z",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12Z Minister may revoke approved ATS marketing plan",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-12z"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.43",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by giving written notice to a primary universal\nservice provider, revoke the provider’s approved ATS marketing\nplan if the Minister considers that it is in the public interest to do\nso. A copy of the notice must be given to the ACA.\n\n(2) An approved ATS marketing plan that is revoked by the Minister\nceases to be in force when the revocation takes effect.\n\n(3) The revocation takes effect on the day specified in the notice which\nmust be on or after the day on which the notice is given to the\nprovider.\n\n(4) The Minister may determine in writing arrangements to deal with\nissues of a transitional nature that may arise as a result of the\nrevocation. A copy of the determination must be:\n\n(a) given to the provider; and\n\n(b) published in the Gazette.\n\n(5) The provider must comply with the arrangements (if any) in a\ndetermination under subsection (4).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by giving written notice to a primary universal\nservice provider, revoke the provider’s approved ATS marketing\nplan if the Minister considers that it is in the public interest to do\nso. A copy of the notice must be given to the ACA.\n\n(2) An approved ATS marketing plan that is revoked by the Minister\nceases to be in force when the revocation takes effect.\n\n(3) The revocation takes effect on the day specified in the notice which\nmust be on or after the day on which the notice is given to the\nprovider.\n\n(4) The Minister may determine in writing arrangements to deal with\nissues of a transitional nature that may arise as a result of the\nrevocation. A copy of the determination must be:\n\n(a) given to the provider; and\n\n(b) published in the Gazette.\n\n(5) The provider must comply with the arrangements (if any) in a\ndetermination under subsection (4).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12z-ss-1"
        },
        {
