    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13A Application to be approved as a competing universal service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "provider\n\n(1) A carrier or carriage service provider may apply to the ACA for\napproval as a competing universal service provider for a universal\nservice area in respect of a contestable service obligation.\n\n(2) The application must be in the form approved in writing by the\nACA and must be accompanied by:\n\n(a) a draft policy statement, or draft variation of an approved\npolicy statement; and\n\n(b) at least one of the following:\n\n(i) a draft standard marketing plan;\n\n(ii) a draft ATS marketing plan; and\n\n(c) such information or documents as are required by the\napproved form.\nNote 1:\nFor the meaning of draft policy statement and approved policy\nstatement, see section 13F.\nNote 2:\nFor the meaning of draft ATS marketing plan, see section 13M.",
      "skos:definition": "provider\n\n(1) A carrier or carriage service provider may apply to the ACA for\napproval as a competing universal service provider for a universal\nservice area in respect of a contestable service obligation.\n\n(2) The application must be in the form approved in writing by the\nACA and must be accompanied by:\n\n(a) a draft policy statement, or draft variation of an approved\npolicy statement; and\n\n(b) at least one of the following:\n\n(i) a draft standard marketing plan;\n\n(ii) a draft ATS marketing plan; and\n\n(c) such information or documents as are required by the\napproved form.\nNote 1:\nFor the meaning of draft policy statement and approved policy\nstatement, see section 13F.\nNote 2:\nFor the meaning of draft ATS marketing plan, see section 13M.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5c4c1964340aca5b65393bbe9d3249cdd71be26665b3320ad694f034f2743283"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13A Application to be approved as a competing universal service",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "provider\n\n(1) A carrier or carriage service provider may apply to the ACA for\napproval as a competing universal service provider for a universal\nservice area in respect of a contestable service obligation.\n\n(2) The application must be in the form approved in writing by the\nACA and must be accompanied by:\n\n(a) a draft policy statement, or draft variation of an approved\npolicy statement; and\n\n(b) at least one of the following:\n\n(i) a draft standard marketing plan;\n\n(ii) a draft ATS marketing plan; and\n\n(c) such information or documents as are required by the\napproved form.\nNote 1:\nFor the meaning of draft policy statement and approved policy\nstatement, see section 13F.\nNote 2:\nFor the meaning of draft ATS marketing plan, see section 13M."
    },
