    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13C Date of effect of approval, or variation or revocation of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "approval\n\n(1) An approval under section 13B takes effect on the day specified in\nthe approval. That day must be on or after the day on which the\napproval is given.\n\n(2) If an approval is expressed to cease to have effect at a specified\ntime, it ceases to have effect at that time.\n\n(3) A variation or revocation of an approval takes effect on the day\nspecified for the purpose in the instrument of variation or\nrevocation. That day must be on or after the day on which the\ninstrument is made.\n\n(4) If the ACA revokes an approval under section 13B, it may\ndetermine in writing arrangements to deal with any issues of a\ntransitional nature that may arise as a result of the revocation.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "approval\n\n(1) An approval under section 13B takes effect on the day specified in\nthe approval. That day must be on or after the day on which the\napproval is given.\n\n(2) If an approval is expressed to cease to have effect at a specified\ntime, it ceases to have effect at that time.\n\n(3) A variation or revocation of an approval takes effect on the day\nspecified for the purpose in the instrument of variation or\nrevocation. That day must be on or after the day on which the\ninstrument is made.\n\n(4) If the ACA revokes an approval under section 13B, it may\ndetermine in writing arrangements to deal with any issues of a\ntransitional nature that may arise as a result of the revocation.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13c-ss-2"
