      "skos:definition": "(4) If the ACA revokes an approval under section 13B, it may\ndetermine in writing arrangements to deal with any issues of a\ntransitional nature that may arise as a result of the revocation.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13c-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "08973f954dcbb23e25542f374630296f5a12ecab61063f42216da43b66cb6af7",
      "skos:note": "Determines arrangements for transitional issues after revocation of approval under section 13B."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13c-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13C(4) Date of effect of approval, or variation or revocation of",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the ACA revokes an approval under section 13B, it may\ndetermine in writing arrangements to deal with any issues of a\ntransitional nature that may arise as a result of the revocation.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
