    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13E Surrender of approval as a competing universal service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "provider\n\n(1) A competing universal service provider for a universal service area\nin respect of a contestable service obligation may, at any time,\nnotify the ACA that the provider intends to cease fulfilling that\ncontestable service obligation, so far as it relates to that area.\n\n(2) In giving the notice to the ACA, the provider must comply with:\n\n(a) the procedures referred to in paragraph 13K(2)(e) set out in\nthe provider’s approved standard marketing plan; or\n\n(b) the procedures referred to in paragraph 13Q(2)(f) set out in\nthe provider’s approved ATS marketing plan;\nwhichever are applicable.\n\n(3) After receiving the notice, the ACA may determine in writing:\n\n(a) the date on which the provider’s approval as a competing\nuniversal service provider in respect of that contestable\nservice obligation ceases to have effect; and\n\n(b) that section 13D does not apply, to the extent specified in the\ndetermination, to the provider from the day on which the\nACA received the notice or a later day specified in the\ndetermination.\n\n(4) A copy of the determination must be:\n\n(a) given to the provider; and\n\n(b) published in the Gazette.\nSubdivision C—Policy statements and standard marketing\nplans of competing universal service providers",
      "skos:definition": "provider\n\n(1) A competing universal service provider for a universal service area\nin respect of a contestable service obligation may, at any time,\nnotify the ACA that the provider intends to cease fulfilling that\ncontestable service obligation, so far as it relates to that area.\n\n(2) In giving the notice to the ACA, the provider must comply with:\n\n(a) the procedures referred to in paragraph 13K(2)(e) set out in\nthe provider’s approved standard marketing plan; or\n\n(b) the procedures referred to in paragraph 13Q(2)(f) set out in\nthe provider’s approved ATS marketing plan;\nwhichever are applicable.\n\n(3) After receiving the notice, the ACA may determine in writing:\n\n(a) the date on which the provider’s approval as a competing\nuniversal service provider in respect of that contestable\nservice obligation ceases to have effect; and\n\n(b) that section 13D does not apply, to the extent specified in the\ndetermination, to the provider from the day on which the\nACA received the notice or a later day specified in the\ndetermination.\n\n(4) A copy of the determination must be:\n\n(a) given to the provider; and\n\n(b) published in the Gazette.\nSubdivision C—Policy statements and standard marketing\nplans of competing universal service providers",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13e-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13e-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13e-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5c4c1964340aca5b65393bbe9d3249cdd71be26665b3320ad694f034f2743283"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13E Surrender of approval as a competing universal service",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 47,
      "values:originalText": "provider\n\n(1) A competing universal service provider for a universal service area\nin respect of a contestable service obligation may, at any time,\nnotify the ACA that the provider intends to cease fulfilling that\ncontestable service obligation, so far as it relates to that area.\n\n(2) In giving the notice to the ACA, the provider must comply with:\n\n(a) the procedures referred to in paragraph 13K(2)(e) set out in\nthe provider’s approved standard marketing plan; or\n\n(b) the procedures referred to in paragraph 13Q(2)(f) set out in\nthe provider’s approved ATS marketing plan;\nwhichever are applicable.\n\n(3) After receiving the notice, the ACA may determine in writing:\n\n(a) the date on which the provider’s approval as a competing\nuniversal service provider in respect of that contestable\nservice obligation ceases to have effect; and\n\n(b) that section 13D does not apply, to the extent specified in the\ndetermination, to the provider from the day on which the\nACA received the notice or a later day specified in the\ndetermination.\n\n(4) A copy of the determination must be:\n\n(a) given to the provider; and\n\n(b) published in the Gazette.\nSubdivision C—Policy statements and standard marketing\nplans of competing universal service providers"
    },
