    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13F Meaning of expressions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A draft policy statement for an applicant for approval as a\ncompeting universal service provider is a general statement of the\npolicy the applicant will apply in supplying equipment, goods or\nservices as a competing universal service provider.\n\n(2) A draft policy statement that has been approved by the ACA under\nsection 13J, and that is in force, is an approved policy statement\nfor the applicant or competing universal service provider\nconcerned.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A draft policy statement for an applicant for approval as a\ncompeting universal service provider is a general statement of the\npolicy the applicant will apply in supplying equipment, goods or\nservices as a competing universal service provider.\n\n(2) A draft policy statement that has been approved by the ACA under\nsection 13J, and that is in force, is an approved policy statement\nfor the applicant or competing universal service provider\nconcerned.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "cml:hasPart": [
