    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13J Approval of draft policy statement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.49",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACA must approve, or refuse to approve, a draft policy\nstatement that an applicant for approval as a competing universal\nservice provider gives to the ACA.\n\n(2) The ACA must not approve the draft unless it is satisfied that the\ndraft adequately deals with the supply of appropriate equipment,\ngoods or services to:\n\n(a) people with a disability; and\n\n(b) people with special needs.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACA must approve, or refuse to approve, a draft policy\nstatement that an applicant for approval as a competing universal\nservice provider gives to the ACA.\n\n(2) The ACA must not approve the draft unless it is satisfied that the\ndraft adequately deals with the supply of appropriate equipment,\ngoods or services to:\n\n(a) people with a disability; and\n\n(b) people with special needs.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13j-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2cec1d99f7a2a21bb99fb9b34cb3fc1658a56c816d14312cf65d57507e88a685"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13J Approval of draft policy statement",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 49,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACA must approve, or refuse to approve, a draft policy\nstatement that an applicant for approval as a competing universal\nservice provider gives to the ACA.\n\n(2) The ACA must not approve the draft unless it is satisfied that the\ndraft adequately deals with the supply of appropriate equipment,\ngoods or services to:\n\n(a) people with a disability; and\n\n(b) people with special needs.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13j-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
