      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The ACA must not approve the draft unless...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...it is satisfied that the draft adequately deals with..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-46",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-46"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n\n(3) The ACA must also be satisfied that the draft sets out appropriate\narrangements that the applicant will put in place if another\ncompeting universal service provider for the universal service area\nconcerned, in respect of the contestable service obligation\nconcerned, ceases to supply equipment, goods or services in that\narea in respect of that contestable service obligation.\nNote:\nThe arrangements may, for example, deal with the transfer of\ncustomers from one competing universal service provider to another.\n\n(4) In deciding whether to approve the draft, the ACA must also have\nregard to:\n\n(a) whether the draft complies with the requirements (if any)\nunder section 13G; and\n\n(b) any other matters determined in writing by the Minister for\nthe purposes of this paragraph; and\n\n(c) such other matters as the ACA considers relevant.\n\n(5) A copy of a determination made for the purposes of\nparagraph (4)(b) must be published in the Gazette.",
      "skos:definition": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n\n(3) The ACA must also be satisfied that the draft sets out appropriate\narrangements that the applicant will put in place if another\ncompeting universal service provider for the universal service area\nconcerned, in respect of the contestable service obligation\nconcerned, ceases to supply equipment, goods or services in that\narea in respect of that contestable service obligation.\nNote:\nThe arrangements may, for example, deal with the transfer of\ncustomers from one competing universal service provider to another.\n\n(4) In deciding whether to approve the draft, the ACA must also have\nregard to:\n\n(a) whether the draft complies with the requirements (if any)\nunder section 13G; and\n\n(b) any other matters determined in writing by the Minister for\nthe purposes of this paragraph; and\n\n(c) such other matters as the ACA considers relevant.\n\n(5) A copy of a determination made for the purposes of\nparagraph (4)(b) must be published in the Gazette.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-46-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-46-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-46-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "979e11152bb97086837bd46c20185accb794ccfc420df3c8dfc17f4413c44d83"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-46",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n\n(3) The ACA must also be satisfied that the draft sets out appropriate\narrangements that the applicant will put in place if another\ncompeting universal service provider for the universal service area\nconcerned, in respect of the contestable service obligation\nconcerned, ceases to supply equipment, goods or services in that\narea in respect of that contestable service obligation.\nNote:\nThe arrangements may, for example, deal with the transfer of\ncustomers from one competing universal service provider to another.\n\n(4) In deciding whether to approve the draft, the ACA must also have\nregard to:\n\n(a) whether the draft complies with the requirements (if any)\nunder section 13G; and\n\n(b) any other matters determined in writing by the Minister for\nthe purposes of this paragraph; and\n\n(c) such other matters as the ACA considers relevant.\n\n(5) A copy of a determination made for the purposes of\nparagraph (4)(b) must be published in the Gazette."
    },
