      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The ACA must not approve the draft unless it is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the draft specifies appropriate equipment, goods or services\nthat the applicant will supply in fulfilment of the contestable\nservice obligation concerned, so far as it relates to the\nuniversal service area concerned; and\n\n(b) the draft adequately deals with how the applicant will fulfil\nthat contestable service obligation, so far as it relates to that\narea; and\n\n(c) the draft sets out appropriate terms and conditions on which\nthe equipment, goods or services are to be supplied; and\n\n(d) the draft sets out appropriate arrangements for the marketing\nof the supply of the equipment, goods or services to persons\nin that area; and\n\n(e) the draft sets out appropriate procedures that the applicant\nwill comply with if the applicant ceases:\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            47\n\n(i) to supply any of the equipment, goods or services; or\n\n(ii) to fulfil that contestable service obligation, so far as it\nrelates to that area;\n\nincluding the giving of at least 45 days’ notice to the ACA,\nor such other notice as the ACA determines in writing is\nadequate."
