    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13M Meaning of expressions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.51",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A draft ATS marketing plan for an applicant for approval as a\ncompeting universal service provider for a universal service area in\nrespect of a contestable service obligation is a plan that sets out:\n\n(a) the alternative telecommunications services that the applicant\nwill supply in fulfilment of that contestable service\nobligation, so far as it relates to that area; and\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A draft ATS marketing plan for an applicant for approval as a\ncompeting universal service provider for a universal service area in\nrespect of a contestable service obligation is a plan that sets out:\n\n(a) the alternative telecommunications services that the applicant\nwill supply in fulfilment of that contestable service\nobligation, so far as it relates to that area; and\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13m-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3f8e3de3d20eaa0aac1e8dd81d0c35141f65f4d1dcebe0807fd9d90d1f1db3ba",
      "skos:note": "Defines a draft ATS marketing plan for an applicant seeking approval as a competing universal service provider."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13M Meaning of expressions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 51,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A draft ATS marketing plan for an applicant for approval as a\ncompeting universal service provider for a universal service area in\nrespect of a contestable service obligation is a plan that sets out:\n\n(a) the alternative telecommunications services that the applicant\nwill supply in fulfilment of that contestable service\nobligation, so far as it relates to that area; and\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13m-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13m"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-48",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-48"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.52",
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n\n(b) the arrangements for supplying and marketing those services.\n\n(2) A draft ATS marketing plan that has been approved by the ACA\nunder section 13Q, and that is in force, is an approved ATS\nmarketing plan for the applicant or competing universal service\nprovider concerned.\n\n(3) Each draft or approved ATS marketing plan must cover only one\nuniversal service area and only one contestable service obligation.\nHowever, the ACA may determine in writing that this subsection\ndoes not apply to:\n\n(a) draft or approved ATS marketing plans generally; or\n\n(b) a draft or approved ATS marketing plan of a particular\napplicant or competing universal service provider.\n\n(4) A copy of a determination made under subsection (3) must be\npublished in the Gazette.",
      "skos:definition": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n\n(b) the arrangements for supplying and marketing those services.\n\n(2) A draft ATS marketing plan that has been approved by the ACA\nunder section 13Q, and that is in force, is an approved ATS\nmarketing plan for the applicant or competing universal service\nprovider concerned.\n\n(3) Each draft or approved ATS marketing plan must cover only one\nuniversal service area and only one contestable service obligation.\nHowever, the ACA may determine in writing that this subsection\ndoes not apply to:\n\n(a) draft or approved ATS marketing plans generally; or\n\n(b) a draft or approved ATS marketing plan of a particular\napplicant or competing universal service provider.\n\n(4) A copy of a determination made under subsection (3) must be\npublished in the Gazette.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-48-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-48-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-48-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "de9940de88c11f9bb4b72d659a7d7138f3f6da0acf58dd853c3b625608321ec0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-48",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 52,
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n\n(b) the arrangements for supplying and marketing those services.\n\n(2) A draft ATS marketing plan that has been approved by the ACA\nunder section 13Q, and that is in force, is an approved ATS\nmarketing plan for the applicant or competing universal service\nprovider concerned.\n\n(3) Each draft or approved ATS marketing plan must cover only one\nuniversal service area and only one contestable service obligation.\nHowever, the ACA may determine in writing that this subsection\ndoes not apply to:\n\n(a) draft or approved ATS marketing plans generally; or\n\n(b) a draft or approved ATS marketing plan of a particular\napplicant or competing universal service provider.\n\n(4) A copy of a determination made under subsection (3) must be\npublished in the Gazette."
    },
    {
