    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13n",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13N Minister may determine requirements for drafts",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13n"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.52",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may determine in writing requirements for draft ATS\nmarketing plans of competing universal service providers.\n\n(2) These are some examples of requirements:\n\n(a) timeframes for the supply of specified equipment, goods or\nservices;\n\n(b) performance standards relating to the fulfilment of the\nuniversal service obligation;\n\n(c) processes for advising persons about the availability, offer\nand supply of equipment, goods or services in the fulfilment\nof the universal service obligation, and the terms and\nconditions on which the equipment, goods or services are\noffered or supplied;\n\n(d) the form of a draft ATS marketing plan.\n\n(3) A determination under this section is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may determine in writing requirements for draft ATS\nmarketing plans of competing universal service providers.\n\n(2) These are some examples of requirements:\n\n(a) timeframes for the supply of specified equipment, goods or\nservices;\n\n(b) performance standards relating to the fulfilment of the\nuniversal service obligation;\n\n(c) processes for advising persons about the availability, offer\nand supply of equipment, goods or services in the fulfilment\nof the universal service obligation, and the terms and\nconditions on which the equipment, goods or services are\noffered or supplied;\n\n(d) the form of a draft ATS marketing plan.\n\n(3) A determination under this section is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13n-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13n-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13n-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "51c17eac09693fcc00192d61b11cce1cf9e33ed295824ff6864105111aa4c4ef"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13n",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13N Minister may determine requirements for drafts",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 52,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may determine in writing requirements for draft ATS\nmarketing plans of competing universal service providers.\n\n(2) These are some examples of requirements:\n\n(a) timeframes for the supply of specified equipment, goods or\nservices;\n\n(b) performance standards relating to the fulfilment of the\nuniversal service obligation;\n\n(c) processes for advising persons about the availability, offer\nand supply of equipment, goods or services in the fulfilment\nof the universal service obligation, and the terms and\nconditions on which the equipment, goods or services are\noffered or supplied;\n\n(d) the form of a draft ATS marketing plan.\n\n(3) A determination under this section is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."
    },
