    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13q",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13Q Approval of draft ATS marketing plan",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13q"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.53",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACA must approve, or refuse to approve, a draft ATS\nmarketing plan that an applicant for approval as a competing\nuniversal service provider gives to the ACA.\n\n(2) The ACA must not approve the draft unless it is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the draft specifies appropriate equipment, goods or services\nthat the applicant will supply in supplying the alternative\ntelecommunications services; and\n\n(b) the draft adequately deals with how the applicant will supply\nalternative telecommunications services in fulfilment of the\ncontestable service obligation concerned, so far as it relates\nto the universal service area concerned; and\n\n(c) the alternative telecommunications services are of general\nappeal and are appropriate for fulfilling that contestable\nservice obligation, so far as it relates to that area; and\n\n(d) the draft sets out appropriate terms and conditions on which\nthe equipment, goods or services are to be supplied; and\n\n(e) the draft sets out appropriate arrangements for the marketing\nof the supply of the equipment, goods or services to persons\nwithin that area; and\n\n(ea) the draft includes a requirement that, before entering into an\nagreement to supply a person with alternative\ntelecommunications services, the provider must give to the\nperson information about the substantive differences\nbetween:\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACA must approve, or refuse to approve, a draft ATS\nmarketing plan that an applicant for approval as a competing\nuniversal service provider gives to the ACA.\n\n(2) The ACA must not approve the draft unless it is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the draft specifies appropriate equipment, goods or services\nthat the applicant will supply in supplying the alternative\ntelecommunications services; and\n\n(b) the draft adequately deals with how the applicant will supply\nalternative telecommunications services in fulfilment of the\ncontestable service obligation concerned, so far as it relates\nto the universal service area concerned; and\n\n(c) the alternative telecommunications services are of general\nappeal and are appropriate for fulfilling that contestable\nservice obligation, so far as it relates to that area; and\n\n(d) the draft sets out appropriate terms and conditions on which\nthe equipment, goods or services are to be supplied; and\n\n(e) the draft sets out appropriate arrangements for the marketing\nof the supply of the equipment, goods or services to persons\nwithin that area; and\n\n(ea) the draft includes a requirement that, before entering into an\nagreement to supply a person with alternative\ntelecommunications services, the provider must give to the\nperson information about the substantive differences\nbetween:\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13q-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13q-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "21f299ff9eaccdb611bce2ed34fa76703e14a55411a0467f9a854c1d745e9206"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13q",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13Q Approval of draft ATS marketing plan",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 53,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACA must approve, or refuse to approve, a draft ATS\nmarketing plan that an applicant for approval as a competing\nuniversal service provider gives to the ACA.\n\n(2) The ACA must not approve the draft unless it is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the draft specifies appropriate equipment, goods or services\nthat the applicant will supply in supplying the alternative\ntelecommunications services; and\n\n(b) the draft adequately deals with how the applicant will supply\nalternative telecommunications services in fulfilment of the\ncontestable service obligation concerned, so far as it relates\nto the universal service area concerned; and\n\n(c) the alternative telecommunications services are of general\nappeal and are appropriate for fulfilling that contestable\nservice obligation, so far as it relates to that area; and\n\n(d) the draft sets out appropriate terms and conditions on which\nthe equipment, goods or services are to be supplied; and\n\n(e) the draft sets out appropriate arrangements for the marketing\nof the supply of the equipment, goods or services to persons\nwithin that area; and\n\n(ea) the draft includes a requirement that, before entering into an\nagreement to supply a person with alternative\ntelecommunications services, the provider must give to the\nperson information about the substantive differences\nbetween:\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
    },
    {
