    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13r",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13R Notice of decision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13r"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.54",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACA must give the applicant written notice of the ACA’s\ndecision on whether to approve the draft ATS marketing plan.\n\n(2) If the ACA refuses to approve the draft, the ACA must give the\napplicant written notice of the reasons for that refusal.\n\n(3) A copy of a notice under subsection (1) must be published in the\nGazette, if the decision is to approve the draft.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            51\nSubdivision E—Replacement, variation and revocation of\npolicy statements, standard marketing plans and\nATS marketing plans",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACA must give the applicant written notice of the ACA’s\ndecision on whether to approve the draft ATS marketing plan.\n\n(2) If the ACA refuses to approve the draft, the ACA must give the\napplicant written notice of the reasons for that refusal.\n\n(3) A copy of a notice under subsection (1) must be published in the\nGazette, if the decision is to approve the draft.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            51\nSubdivision E—Replacement, variation and revocation of\npolicy statements, standard marketing plans and\nATS marketing plans",
