        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "669de56158c34ccc1a4c6a047420e99252318118d4ee37a4a7de8edcda59f9d7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-13t",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13T Variation of approved policy statement, approved standard",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 55,
      "values:originalText": "marketing plan or approved ATS marketing plan\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an approved policy statement for a competing universal\nservice provider (the current statement) is in force; or\n\n(b) an approved standard marketing plan for a competing\nuniversal service provider (the current plan) is in force; or\n\n(c) an approved ATS marketing plan for a competing universal\nservice provider (the current plan) is in force;\nand the provider gives the ACA a draft variation of the current\nstatement or current plan.\n\n(2) The ACA must:\n\n(a) approve the variation; or\n\n(b) refuse to approve the variation.\n\n(3) Before deciding whether to approve the variation, the ACA may, if\nthe ACA considers it appropriate, require the provider:\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
    },
