    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-52",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-52"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n\n(a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft variation and\ninvite members of the public to make submissions to the\nprovider about the preliminary version within a specified\nperiod; and\n\n(b) to give consideration to any submissions from members of\nthe public received within that period; and\n\n(c) to advise the ACA on those submissions and any changes\nmade to the draft variation as a result.\n\n(4) The ACA must not approve the variation unless it is satisfied that:\n\n(a) in the case of a draft variation of an approved policy\nstatement—if the provider were to give the ACA a draft\npolicy statement in the same terms as the current statement as\nvaried, the ACA would approve that draft; or\n\n(b) in the case of a draft variation of an approved standard\nmarketing plan—if the provider were to give the ACA a draft\nstandard marketing plan in the same terms as the current plan\nas varied, the ACA would approve that draft; or\n\n(c) in the case of a draft variation of an approved ATS marketing\nplan—if the provider were to give the ACA a draft ATS\nmarketing plan in the same terms as the current plan as\nvaried, the ACA would approve that draft.",
      "skos:definition": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n\n(a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft variation and\ninvite members of the public to make submissions to the\nprovider about the preliminary version within a specified\nperiod; and\n\n(b) to give consideration to any submissions from members of\nthe public received within that period; and\n\n(c) to advise the ACA on those submissions and any changes\nmade to the draft variation as a result.\n\n(4) The ACA must not approve the variation unless it is satisfied that:\n\n(a) in the case of a draft variation of an approved policy\nstatement—if the provider were to give the ACA a draft\npolicy statement in the same terms as the current statement as\nvaried, the ACA would approve that draft; or\n\n(b) in the case of a draft variation of an approved standard\nmarketing plan—if the provider were to give the ACA a draft\nstandard marketing plan in the same terms as the current plan\nas varied, the ACA would approve that draft; or\n\n(c) in the case of a draft variation of an approved ATS marketing\nplan—if the provider were to give the ACA a draft ATS\nmarketing plan in the same terms as the current plan as\nvaried, the ACA would approve that draft.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-52-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-52-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8958fd993202fac5171011d0dc85c874a6887a241193c875fff2a840d4872b5b",
      "skos:note": "Provider must give consideration to public submissions on preliminary variation draft.",
      "dc:description": "Submissions from members of the public"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-52",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 56,
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n\n(a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft variation and\ninvite members of the public to make submissions to the\nprovider about the preliminary version within a specified\nperiod; and\n\n(b) to give consideration to any submissions from members of\nthe public received within that period; and\n\n(c) to advise the ACA on those submissions and any changes\nmade to the draft variation as a result.\n\n(4) The ACA must not approve the variation unless it is satisfied that:\n\n(a) in the case of a draft variation of an approved policy\nstatement—if the provider were to give the ACA a draft\npolicy statement in the same terms as the current statement as\nvaried, the ACA would approve that draft; or\n\n(b) in the case of a draft variation of an approved standard\nmarketing plan—if the provider were to give the ACA a draft\nstandard marketing plan in the same terms as the current plan\nas varied, the ACA would approve that draft; or\n\n(c) in the case of a draft variation of an approved ATS marketing\nplan—if the provider were to give the ACA a draft ATS\nmarketing plan in the same terms as the current plan as\nvaried, the ACA would approve that draft."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-52-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-52"
