    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-14a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14A Effect of determination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-14a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.58",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A determination under section 14 takes effect on the day specified\nin the determination. That day must not be before the day on which\nnotice of the determination is published in the Gazette.\n\n(2) If a determination under section 14 is expressed to cease to have\neffect at a specified time, the determination ceases to have effect at\nthat time.\n\n(3) A variation or revocation of a determination under section 14 takes\neffect on the day specified for the purpose in the instrument of\nvariation or revocation. That day must not be before notice of the\ninstrument is published in the Gazette.\n\n(4) If the Minister revokes a determination under section 14, the\nMinister may determine in writing arrangements to deal with any\nissues of a transitional nature that may arise as a result of the\nrevocation.\n\n(5) A copy of a determination under subsection (4) must be published\nin the Gazette.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A determination under section 14 takes effect on the day specified\nin the determination. That day must not be before the day on which\nnotice of the determination is published in the Gazette.\n\n(2) If a determination under section 14 is expressed to cease to have\neffect at a specified time, the determination ceases to have effect at\nthat time.\n\n(3) A variation or revocation of a determination under section 14 takes\neffect on the day specified for the purpose in the instrument of\nvariation or revocation. That day must not be before notice of the\ninstrument is published in the Gazette.\n\n(4) If the Minister revokes a determination under section 14, the\nMinister may determine in writing arrangements to deal with any\nissues of a transitional nature that may arise as a result of the\nrevocation.\n\n(5) A copy of a determination under subsection (4) must be published\nin the Gazette.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-14a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-14a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-14a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-14a-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-14a-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e5984f9bea34f4da06c8cd0351365a37796231aaeba7f7da86334896e11db2d3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-14a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14A Effect of determination",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 58,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A determination under section 14 takes effect on the day specified\nin the determination. That day must not be before the day on which\nnotice of the determination is published in the Gazette.\n\n(2) If a determination under section 14 is expressed to cease to have\neffect at a specified time, the determination ceases to have effect at\nthat time.\n\n(3) A variation or revocation of a determination under section 14 takes\neffect on the day specified for the purpose in the instrument of\nvariation or revocation. That day must not be before notice of the\ninstrument is published in the Gazette.\n\n(4) If the Minister revokes a determination under section 14, the\nMinister may determine in writing arrangements to deal with any\nissues of a transitional nature that may arise as a result of the\nrevocation.\n\n(5) A copy of a determination under subsection (4) must be published\nin the Gazette."
    },
