    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15b-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15B(7) Former digital data service provider may be required to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15b-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.60",
      "values:originalText": "(7) If a requirement made by a notice under subsection (5) is\nreasonable, the former provider must comply with the requirement\nas soon as practicable after receiving the notice. However, if the\nrequirement is unreasonable, the former provider does not have to\ncomply with it.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "(7) If a requirement made by a notice under subsection (5) is\nreasonable, the former provider must comply with the requirement\nas soon as practicable after receiving the notice. However, if the\nrequirement is unreasonable, the former provider does not have to\ncomply with it.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15b-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15b-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b2effa3e138609d565c4a7c3cc3b9f321b3d99ba3c6ced45eccdc6b954295fb4",
      "skos:note": "Must comply with reasonable requirements after receiving notice.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15b-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15B(7) Former digital data service provider may be required to",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 60,
      "values:originalText": "(7) If a requirement made by a notice under subsection (5) is\nreasonable, the former provider must comply with the requirement\nas soon as practicable after receiving the notice. However, if the\nrequirement is unreasonable, the former provider does not have to\ncomply with it.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
    },
