    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15D Digital data service plans",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "A draft or approved digital data service plan for an area is a plan\nthat sets out how a digital data service provider for that area will\nprogressively fulfil:\n\n(a) if that area is a general digital data service area—the general\ndigital data service obligation (in so far as the obligation\nrelates to that area); or\n\n(b) if that area is a special digital data service area—the special\ndigital data service obligation (in so far as the obligation\nrelates to that area).\nNote:\nAn approved digital data service plan is a draft digital data service\nplan that has been approved by the Minister.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            59",
      "skos:definition": "A draft or approved digital data service plan for an area is a plan\nthat sets out how a digital data service provider for that area will\nprogressively fulfil:\n\n(a) if that area is a general digital data service area—the general\ndigital data service obligation (in so far as the obligation\nrelates to that area); or\n\n(b) if that area is a special digital data service area—the special\ndigital data service obligation (in so far as the obligation\nrelates to that area).\nNote:\nAn approved digital data service plan is a draft digital data service\nplan that has been approved by the Minister.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            59",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15d-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15d-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e893029cf0e49c786f7238f7d2a9f722db0d1b51da1f40163d184a1eaeb06c1e",
      "skos:note": "Sets out how a digital data service provider will progressively fulfil the general or special digital data service obligation in that area."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15D Digital data service plans",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "A draft or approved digital data service plan for an area is a plan\nthat sets out how a digital data service provider for that area will\nprogressively fulfil:\n\n(a) if that area is a general digital data service area—the general\ndigital data service obligation (in so far as the obligation\nrelates to that area); or\n\n(b) if that area is a special digital data service area—the special\ndigital data service obligation (in so far as the obligation\nrelates to that area).\nNote:\nAn approved digital data service plan is a draft digital data service\nplan that has been approved by the Minister.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            59"
    },
