    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15G Public consultation—draft plan",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.63",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before giving the Minister a draft digital data service plan under\nsection 15F, a digital data service provider must:\n\n(a) publish a preliminary version of the draft plan and invite\nmembers of the public to make submissions to the provider\nabout the preliminary version within a specified period; and\n\n(b) give consideration to any submissions received from\nmembers of the public within that period.\n\n(2) The period specified in the invitation must run for at least 30 days.\n\n(3) This section does not apply to a draft plan given to the Minister in\naccordance with a direction under subsection 15F(3).\n\n(4) This section does not apply to a draft plan given to the Minister in\naccordance with a notice under paragraph 15N(2)(b).\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Before giving the Minister a draft digital data service plan under\nsection 15F, a digital data service provider must:\n\n(a) publish a preliminary version of the draft plan and invite\nmembers of the public to make submissions to the provider\nabout the preliminary version within a specified period; and\n\n(b) give consideration to any submissions received from\nmembers of the public within that period.\n\n(2) The period specified in the invitation must run for at least 30 days.\n\n(3) This section does not apply to a draft plan given to the Minister in\naccordance with a direction under subsection 15F(3).\n\n(4) This section does not apply to a draft plan given to the Minister in\naccordance with a notice under paragraph 15N(2)(b).\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15g-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15g-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15g-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "51d2c14145407f8e697a674574c9e15ea631f2c0bb7e9daeec0e3c6beb13c6c6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15G Public consultation—draft plan",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 63,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before giving the Minister a draft digital data service plan under\nsection 15F, a digital data service provider must:\n\n(a) publish a preliminary version of the draft plan and invite\nmembers of the public to make submissions to the provider\nabout the preliminary version within a specified period; and\n\n(b) give consideration to any submissions received from\nmembers of the public within that period.\n\n(2) The period specified in the invitation must run for at least 30 days.\n\n(3) This section does not apply to a draft plan given to the Minister in\naccordance with a direction under subsection 15F(3).\n\n(4) This section does not apply to a draft plan given to the Minister in\naccordance with a notice under paragraph 15N(2)(b).\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
    },
