    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15H Minister to have regard to certain matters",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In deciding whether to approve a draft digital data service plan for\na general digital data service area or a special digital data service\narea, the Minister must have regard to whether:\n\n(a) the draft plan provides for the general digital data service\nobligation, or special digital data service obligation, (so far as\nit relates to that area) to be fulfilled:\n\n(i) as efficiently and economically as practicable; and\n\n(ii) at performance standards that reasonably meet the\nsocial, industrial and commercial needs of the\nAustralian community; and\n\n(iii) progressively throughout that area within such period as\nthe Minister considers reasonable; and\n\n(aa) the draft plan addresses the needs of people with a disability;\nand\n\n(b) the draft plan complies with any requirements in force under\nsection 15J.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which\nregard may be had.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In deciding whether to approve a draft digital data service plan for\na general digital data service area or a special digital data service\narea, the Minister must have regard to whether:\n\n(a) the draft plan provides for the general digital data service\nobligation, or special digital data service obligation, (so far as\nit relates to that area) to be fulfilled:\n\n(i) as efficiently and economically as practicable; and\n\n(ii) at performance standards that reasonably meet the\nsocial, industrial and commercial needs of the\nAustralian community; and\n\n(iii) progressively throughout that area within such period as\nthe Minister considers reasonable; and\n\n(aa) the draft plan addresses the needs of people with a disability;\nand\n\n(b) the draft plan complies with any requirements in force under\nsection 15J.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which\nregard may be had.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15h-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "16ba55d71067c7abef9a5a5f83e9e7b5b4b50808f26da152ce421e26c35e44af"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15H Minister to have regard to certain matters",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In deciding whether to approve a draft digital data service plan for\na general digital data service area or a special digital data service\narea, the Minister must have regard to whether:\n\n(a) the draft plan provides for the general digital data service\nobligation, or special digital data service obligation, (so far as\nit relates to that area) to be fulfilled:\n\n(i) as efficiently and economically as practicable; and\n\n(ii) at performance standards that reasonably meet the\nsocial, industrial and commercial needs of the\nAustralian community; and\n\n(iii) progressively throughout that area within such period as\nthe Minister considers reasonable; and\n\n(aa) the draft plan addresses the needs of people with a disability;\nand\n\n(b) the draft plan complies with any requirements in force under\nsection 15J.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which\nregard may be had."
    },
