      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In deciding whether to approve a draft digital data service plan for\na general digital data service area or a special digital data service\narea, the Minister must have regard to whether:\n\n(a) the draft plan provides for the general digital data service\nobligation, or special digital data service obligation, (so far as\nit relates to that area) to be fulfilled:\n\n(i) as efficiently and economically as practicable; and\n\n(ii) at performance standards that reasonably meet the\nsocial, industrial and commercial needs of the\nAustralian community; and\n\n(iii) progressively throughout that area within such period as\nthe Minister considers reasonable; and\n\n(aa) the draft plan addresses the needs of people with a disability;\nand\n\n(b) the draft plan complies with any requirements in force under\nsection 15J."
