    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15J Minister may formulate requirements for draft plans",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by writing, formulate requirements for draft\ndigital data service plans.\n\n(2) The following are examples of requirements:\n\n(a) timetables for the supply of services;\n\n(b) performance standards relating to the fulfilment of the digital\ndata service obligation;\n\n(c) the form of a draft digital data service plan.\n\n(3) An instrument under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by writing, formulate requirements for draft\ndigital data service plans.\n\n(2) The following are examples of requirements:\n\n(a) timetables for the supply of services;\n\n(b) performance standards relating to the fulfilment of the digital\ndata service obligation;\n\n(c) the form of a draft digital data service plan.\n\n(3) An instrument under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15j-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15j-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "92cc4aa331378b7f5463696381227ee07fb46d11e87702b16374af83d866a216"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15J Minister may formulate requirements for draft plans",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by writing, formulate requirements for draft\ndigital data service plans.\n\n(2) The following are examples of requirements:\n\n(a) timetables for the supply of services;\n\n(b) performance standards relating to the fulfilment of the digital\ndata service obligation;\n\n(c) the form of a draft digital data service plan.\n\n(3) An instrument under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."
    },
