    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15k",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15K Notification of decision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15k"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "(1) After deciding whether to approve a draft digital data service plan\nfor an area, the Minister must give a written notice setting out the\ndecision to:\n\n(a) the digital data service provider concerned; and\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            61\n\n(b) the ACA.\n\n(2) A copy of a notice under subsection (1) must be published in the\nGazette.\n\n(3) If the Minister refuses to approve a draft digital data service plan\nfor an area, the Minister must give a written notice setting out the\nreasons for the refusal to the digital data service provider\nconcerned.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) After deciding whether to approve a draft digital data service plan\nfor an area, the Minister must give a written notice setting out the\ndecision to:\n\n(a) the digital data service provider concerned; and\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            61\n\n(b) the ACA.\n\n(2) A copy of a notice under subsection (1) must be published in the\nGazette.\n\n(3) If the Minister refuses to approve a draft digital data service plan\nfor an area, the Minister must give a written notice setting out the\nreasons for the refusal to the digital data service provider\nconcerned.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15k-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15k-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15k-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "96c94b71a7b4d6ce21a54a3c5c28c16373772edc8b6b28bd4866c3ad288f2901"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15k",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15K Notification of decision",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(1) After deciding whether to approve a draft digital data service plan\nfor an area, the Minister must give a written notice setting out the\ndecision to:\n\n(a) the digital data service provider concerned; and\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            61\n\n(b) the ACA.\n\n(2) A copy of a notice under subsection (1) must be published in the\nGazette.\n\n(3) If the Minister refuses to approve a draft digital data service plan\nfor an area, the Minister must give a written notice setting out the\nreasons for the refusal to the digital data service provider\nconcerned."
    },
