    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15L Variation of approved digital data service plan",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.65",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an approved digital data service plan for an area (the current\nplan) is in force; and\n\n(b) the digital data service provider concerned gives the Minister\na draft variation of the plan.\n\n(2) The Minister must:\n\n(a) approve the variation; or\n\n(b) refuse to approve the variation.\n\n(3) Before deciding whether to approve the variation, the Minister\nmay, if he or she considers it appropriate, require the provider:\n\n(a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft variation and\ninvite members of the public to make submissions to the\nprovider about the preliminary version within a specified\nperiod; and\n\n(b) to give consideration to any submissions from members of\nthe public received within that period; and\n\n(c) to advise the Minister on those submissions and any changes\nmade to the draft variation as a result.\n\n(4) The Minister must not approve the variation unless the Minister is\nsatisfied that, if the provider were to give the Minister a draft\ndigital data service plan in the same terms as the current plan as\nproposed to be varied, the Minister would approve that draft.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an approved digital data service plan for an area (the current\nplan) is in force; and\n\n(b) the digital data service provider concerned gives the Minister\na draft variation of the plan.\n\n(2) The Minister must:\n\n(a) approve the variation; or\n\n(b) refuse to approve the variation.\n\n(3) Before deciding whether to approve the variation, the Minister\nmay, if he or she considers it appropriate, require the provider:\n\n(a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft variation and\ninvite members of the public to make submissions to the\nprovider about the preliminary version within a specified\nperiod; and\n\n(b) to give consideration to any submissions from members of\nthe public received within that period; and\n\n(c) to advise the Minister on those submissions and any changes\nmade to the draft variation as a result.\n\n(4) The Minister must not approve the variation unless the Minister is\nsatisfied that, if the provider were to give the Minister a draft\ndigital data service plan in the same terms as the current plan as\nproposed to be varied, the Minister would approve that draft.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15l-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15l-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15l-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15l-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "be4fa3c6a6cafd06680097c193cf0a99764422d6e3e687f272fb9b48cad34bbf"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15l",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15L Variation of approved digital data service plan",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 65,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an approved digital data service plan for an area (the current\nplan) is in force; and\n\n(b) the digital data service provider concerned gives the Minister\na draft variation of the plan.\n\n(2) The Minister must:\n\n(a) approve the variation; or\n\n(b) refuse to approve the variation.\n\n(3) Before deciding whether to approve the variation, the Minister\nmay, if he or she considers it appropriate, require the provider:\n\n(a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft variation and\ninvite members of the public to make submissions to the\nprovider about the preliminary version within a specified\nperiod; and\n\n(b) to give consideration to any submissions from members of\nthe public received within that period; and\n\n(c) to advise the Minister on those submissions and any changes\nmade to the draft variation as a result.\n\n(4) The Minister must not approve the variation unless the Minister is\nsatisfied that, if the provider were to give the Minister a draft\ndigital data service plan in the same terms as the current plan as\nproposed to be varied, the Minister would approve that draft."
    },
