    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15n",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15N Minister may direct variation or replacement of plan",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15n"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an approved digital data service plan (the\ncurrent plan) for an area is in force.\n\n(2) The Minister may give the digital data service provider concerned\na written notice requiring the provider:\n\n(a) within the period and in the terms set out in the notice, to\ngive the Minister a draft variation of the current plan; or\n\n(b) within the period and in the terms set out in the notice, to\ngive the Minister a fresh draft digital data service plan for the\narea that is expressed to replace the current plan.\n\n(3) The provider must comply with the notice.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if an approved digital data service plan (the\ncurrent plan) for an area is in force.\n\n(2) The Minister may give the digital data service provider concerned\na written notice requiring the provider:\n\n(a) within the period and in the terms set out in the notice, to\ngive the Minister a draft variation of the current plan; or\n\n(b) within the period and in the terms set out in the notice, to\ngive the Minister a fresh draft digital data service plan for the\narea that is expressed to replace the current plan.\n\n(3) The provider must comply with the notice.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15n-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15n-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15n-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "92373b5ee917e3182d7376daecfcbe7e15dd01a0b1691775f7e0f96846ad143a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-15n",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15N Minister may direct variation or replacement of plan",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an approved digital data service plan (the\ncurrent plan) for an area is in force.\n\n(2) The Minister may give the digital data service provider concerned\na written notice requiring the provider:\n\n(a) within the period and in the terms set out in the notice, to\ngive the Minister a draft variation of the current plan; or\n\n(b) within the period and in the terms set out in the notice, to\ngive the Minister a fresh draft digital data service plan for the\narea that is expressed to replace the current plan.\n\n(3) The provider must comply with the notice."
    },
