    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-16-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16 Determination of universal service subsidy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-16-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before the end of a claim period, the Minister must determine in\nwriting one or more universal service subsidies for the period. A\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            63\ncopy of a determination under this subsection must be published in\nthe Gazette.\n\n(2) The Minister must ensure that there is a subsidy for each universal\nservice area in respect of each service obligation. A subsidy may\ncover one or more universal service areas in respect of one or more\nservice obligations.\n\n(3) A determination under this section must specify:\n\n(a) the amount, or a method for working out the amount, of the\nsubsidy; and\n\n(b) the circumstances in which a universal service provider for\nthe claim period is eligible to be paid the subsidy.\n\n(4) The circumstances that may be specified include, but are not\nlimited to:\n\n(a) whether the subsidy is payable to a primary universal service\nprovider or a competing universal service provider; and\n\n(b) the types or amount of equipment, goods or services that are\nsupplied to persons in a universal service area.\n\n(5) The determination must specify that a subsidy is only payable to a\nuniversal service provider who complies with the provider’s\nobligations under section 12C or 13D (whichever is applicable).\n\n(6) A determination may specify an amount of subsidy as zero.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Before the end of a claim period, the Minister must determine in\nwriting one or more universal service subsidies for the period. A\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            63\ncopy of a determination under this subsection must be published in\nthe Gazette.\n\n(2) The Minister must ensure that there is a subsidy for each universal\nservice area in respect of each service obligation. A subsidy may\ncover one or more universal service areas in respect of one or more\nservice obligations.\n\n(3) A determination under this section must specify:\n\n(a) the amount, or a method for working out the amount, of the\nsubsidy; and\n\n(b) the circumstances in which a universal service provider for\nthe claim period is eligible to be paid the subsidy.\n\n(4) The circumstances that may be specified include, but are not\nlimited to:\n\n(a) whether the subsidy is payable to a primary universal service\nprovider or a competing universal service provider; and\n\n(b) the types or amount of equipment, goods or services that are\nsupplied to persons in a universal service area.\n\n(5) The determination must specify that a subsidy is only payable to a\nuniversal service provider who complies with the provider’s\nobligations under section 12C or 13D (whichever is applicable).\n\n(6) A determination may specify an amount of subsidy as zero.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-16-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-16-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-16-2-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-16-2-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-16-2-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-16-2-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ce3c15f81ab55c84f9fa4d162f35ead256a1377b4d4da253b526b81fa34fdd62"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-16-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16 Determination of universal service subsidy",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before the end of a claim period, the Minister must determine in\nwriting one or more universal service subsidies for the period. A\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            63\ncopy of a determination under this subsection must be published in\nthe Gazette.\n\n(2) The Minister must ensure that there is a subsidy for each universal\nservice area in respect of each service obligation. A subsidy may\ncover one or more universal service areas in respect of one or more\nservice obligations.\n\n(3) A determination under this section must specify:\n\n(a) the amount, or a method for working out the amount, of the\nsubsidy; and\n\n(b) the circumstances in which a universal service provider for\nthe claim period is eligible to be paid the subsidy.\n\n(4) The circumstances that may be specified include, but are not\nlimited to:\n\n(a) whether the subsidy is payable to a primary universal service\nprovider or a competing universal service provider; and\n\n(b) the types or amount of equipment, goods or services that are\nsupplied to persons in a universal service area.\n\n(5) The determination must specify that a subsidy is only payable to a\nuniversal service provider who complies with the provider’s\nobligations under section 12C or 13D (whichever is applicable).\n\n(6) A determination may specify an amount of subsidy as zero."
    },
    {
