    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-16a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16A Minister must seek ACA’s advice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-16a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.67",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before making or varying a determination under section 16, the\nMinister must direct the ACA to give the Minister advice about the\nproposed determination or variation. However, this subsection does\nnot apply to a proposed variation of a minor technical nature.\n\n(2) The ACA must comply with the direction.\n\n(3) If the Minister has received advice from the ACA about a proposed\ndetermination or variation and does not make the determination or\nvariation in accordance with the advice, the Minister must ensure\nthat a notice of his or her reasons for departing from the advice:\n\n(a) is published in the Gazette within 14 days after making the\ndetermination or variation; and\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Before making or varying a determination under section 16, the\nMinister must direct the ACA to give the Minister advice about the\nproposed determination or variation. However, this subsection does\nnot apply to a proposed variation of a minor technical nature.\n\n(2) The ACA must comply with the direction.\n\n(3) If the Minister has received advice from the ACA about a proposed\ndetermination or variation and does not make the determination or\nvariation in accordance with the advice, the Minister must ensure\nthat a notice of his or her reasons for departing from the advice:\n\n(a) is published in the Gazette within 14 days after making the\ndetermination or variation; and\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-16a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-16a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-16a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "176e380e8ca0e1eba36d7d364932bedf8a873a7408587f21e9e4d0cc0d3aeede"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-16a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16A Minister must seek ACA’s advice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 67,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before making or varying a determination under section 16, the\nMinister must direct the ACA to give the Minister advice about the\nproposed determination or variation. However, this subsection does\nnot apply to a proposed variation of a minor technical nature.\n\n(2) The ACA must comply with the direction.\n\n(3) If the Minister has received advice from the ACA about a proposed\ndetermination or variation and does not make the determination or\nvariation in accordance with the advice, the Minister must ensure\nthat a notice of his or her reasons for departing from the advice:\n\n(a) is published in the Gazette within 14 days after making the\ndetermination or variation; and\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
    },
