    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-17",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17 Digital data cost of a digital data service provider for a claim",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-17"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "period\n\n(1) A person’s digital data cost for a claim period depends on which of\nthe following paragraphs is applicable for that claim period:\n\n(a) if:\n\n(i) the person is a digital data service provider for that\nclaim period; and\n\n(ii) a determination is in force under subsection (4) in\nrelation to that claim period;\n\nthe person’s digital data cost for the claim period is worked\nout in accordance with the determination;\n\n(b) if:\n\n(i) the person is a digital data service provider for that\nclaim period; and\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            65\n\n(ii) no determination is in force under subsection (4) in\nrelation to that claim period;\n\nthen:\n\n(iii) if the amount worked out using the formula in\nsubsection (2) is greater than zero—the person’s digital\ndata cost for the claim period is equal to that amount; or\n\n(iv) if the amount worked out using the formula in\nsubsection (2) is not greater than zero—the person’s\ndigital data cost for the claim period is zero.\nNote:\nThe digital data cost is needed for the purposes of making a claim for\nlevy credit for a claim period (see section 20J).\n\n(2) The formula referred to in paragraph (1)(b) is as follows:\nCustomer\nequipment costs\nCustomer charges\nSupplementary amount\n–\n+\n\nwhere:\ncustomer charges means the total amount payable by persons in\nthe area referred to in subsection (3) by way of charges for the\nsupply by the person during the claim period of customer\nequipment covered by paragraph (3)(a).\ncustomer equipment costs means the person’s customer equipment\ncosts for the claim period.\nsupplementary amount means the amount (if any) specified in, or\nascertained in accordance with, regulations made for the purposes\nof this definition.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, if a person is a digital data service\nprovider for an area for a claim period, the person’s customer\nequipment costs for the claim period is an amount equal to the sum\nof:\n\n(a) the total costs incurred by the person in acquiring customer\nequipment that:\n\n(i) is covered by a determination that was in force under\nsection 19A during the claim period in relation to\ncharges imposed, or proposed to be imposed, by the\nperson for the supply of customer equipment of a kind\nspecified in regulations made for the purposes of\nparagraph 10F(1)(a) or 10G(1)(a); and\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "period\n\n(1) A person’s digital data cost for a claim period depends on which of\nthe following paragraphs is applicable for that claim period:\n\n(a) if:\n\n(i) the person is a digital data service provider for that\nclaim period; and\n\n(ii) a determination is in force under subsection (4) in\nrelation to that claim period;\n\nthe person’s digital data cost for the claim period is worked\nout in accordance with the determination;\n\n(b) if:\n\n(i) the person is a digital data service provider for that\nclaim period; and\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            65\n\n(ii) no determination is in force under subsection (4) in\nrelation to that claim period;\n\nthen:\n\n(iii) if the amount worked out using the formula in\nsubsection (2) is greater than zero—the person’s digital\ndata cost for the claim period is equal to that amount; or\n\n(iv) if the amount worked out using the formula in\nsubsection (2) is not greater than zero—the person’s\ndigital data cost for the claim period is zero.\nNote:\nThe digital data cost is needed for the purposes of making a claim for\nlevy credit for a claim period (see section 20J).\n\n(2) The formula referred to in paragraph (1)(b) is as follows:\nCustomer\nequipment costs\nCustomer charges\nSupplementary amount\n–\n+\n\nwhere:\ncustomer charges means the total amount payable by persons in\nthe area referred to in subsection (3) by way of charges for the\nsupply by the person during the claim period of customer\nequipment covered by paragraph (3)(a).\ncustomer equipment costs means the person’s customer equipment\ncosts for the claim period.\nsupplementary amount means the amount (if any) specified in, or\nascertained in accordance with, regulations made for the purposes\nof this definition.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, if a person is a digital data service\nprovider for an area for a claim period, t",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-17-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-17-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-17-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "514cb13f603464f97849ba88d2d4f9698003a9323de9b7a3d162ef76f6998122"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17 Digital data cost of a digital data service provider for a claim",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "period\n\n(1) A person’s digital data cost for a claim period depends on which of\nthe following paragraphs is applicable for that claim period:\n\n(a) if:\n\n(i) the person is a digital data service provider for that\nclaim period; and\n\n(ii) a determination is in force under subsection (4) in\nrelation to that claim period;\n\nthe person’s digital data cost for the claim period is worked\nout in accordance with the determination;\n\n(b) if:\n\n(i) the person is a digital data service provider for that\nclaim period; and\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            65\n\n(ii) no determination is in force under subsection (4) in\nrelation to that claim period;\n\nthen:\n\n(iii) if the amount worked out using the formula in\nsubsection (2) is greater than zero—the person’s digital\ndata cost for the claim period is equal to that amount; or\n\n(iv) if the amount worked out using the formula in\nsubsection (2) is not greater than zero—the person’s\ndigital data cost for the claim period is zero.\nNote:\nThe digital data cost is needed for the purposes of making a claim for\nlevy credit for a claim period (see section 20J).\n\n(2) The formula referred to in paragraph (1)(b) is as follows:\nCustomer\nequipment costs\nCustomer charges\nSupplementary amount\n–\n+\n\nwhere:\ncustomer charges means the total amount payable by persons in\nthe area referred to in subsection (3) by way of charges for the\nsupply by the person during the claim period of customer\nequipment covered by paragraph (3)(a).\ncustomer equipment costs means the person’s customer equipment\ncosts for the claim period.\nsupplementary amount means the amount (if any) specified in, or\nascertained in accordance with, regulations made for the purposes\nof this definition.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, if a person is a digital data service\nprovider for an area for a claim period, the person’s customer\nequipment costs for the claim period is an amount equal to the sum\nof:\n\n(a) the total costs incurred by the person in acquiring customer\nequipment that:\n\n(i) is covered by a determination that was in force under\nsection 19A during the claim period in relation to\ncharges imposed, or proposed to be imposed, by the\nperson for the supply of customer equipment of a kind\nspecified in regulations made for the purposes of\nparagraph 10F(1)(a) or 10G(1)(a); and\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
    },
    {
