    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-17-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17(3) Digital data cost of a digital data service provider for a claim",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-17-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of this section, if a person is a digital data service\nprovider for an area for a claim period, the person’s customer\nequipment costs for the claim period is an amount equal to the sum\nof:\n\n(a) the total costs incurred by the person in acquiring customer\nequipment that:\n\n(i) is covered by a determination that was in force under\nsection 19A during the claim period in relation to\ncharges imposed, or proposed to be imposed, by the\nperson for the supply of customer equipment of a kind\nspecified in regulations made for the purposes of\nparagraph 10F(1)(a) or 10G(1)(a); and\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "(3) For the purposes of this section, if a person is a digital data service\nprovider for an area for a claim period, the person’s customer\nequipment costs for the claim period is an amount equal to the sum\nof:\n\n(a) the total costs incurred by the person in acquiring customer\nequipment that:\n\n(i) is covered by a determination that was in force under\nsection 19A during the claim period in relation to\ncharges imposed, or proposed to be imposed, by the\nperson for the supply of customer equipment of a kind\nspecified in regulations made for the purposes of\nparagraph 10F(1)(a) or 10G(1)(a); and\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-17"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-17-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-17-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9c8550c6aa7ace873c3da73bc6e737122abd53fb84eedb8b0837594b68999637",
      "skos:note": "Digital data service provider's customer equipment costs for a claim period"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-17-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17(3) Digital data cost of a digital data service provider for a claim",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of this section, if a person is a digital data service\nprovider for an area for a claim period, the person’s customer\nequipment costs for the claim period is an amount equal to the sum\nof:\n\n(a) the total costs incurred by the person in acquiring customer\nequipment that:\n\n(i) is covered by a determination that was in force under\nsection 19A during the claim period in relation to\ncharges imposed, or proposed to be imposed, by the\nperson for the supply of customer equipment of a kind\nspecified in regulations made for the purposes of\nparagraph 10F(1)(a) or 10G(1)(a); and\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
    },
