    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-17a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17A Reduction of excessive costs",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-17a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.70",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, formulate principles or\nrules that are to be applied in determining the extent (if any) to\nwhich costs are to be treated as excessive for the purposes of\nsubsection 17(3).\n\n(2) For the purposes of the application of subsection 17(3) in relation\nto a particular claim period, if:\n\n(a) a person has incurred costs of a kind mentioned in paragraph\n17(3)(a); and\n\n(b) the costs are treated, under the principles or rules in force\nunder subsection (1), as excessive to any extent;\nthe amount of the costs is to be reduced by the amount of the\nexcess.\n\n(3) An instrument under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, formulate principles or\nrules that are to be applied in determining the extent (if any) to\nwhich costs are to be treated as excessive for the purposes of\nsubsection 17(3).\n\n(2) For the purposes of the application of subsection 17(3) in relation\nto a particular claim period, if:\n\n(a) a person has incurred costs of a kind mentioned in paragraph\n17(3)(a); and\n\n(b) the costs are treated, under the principles or rules in force\nunder subsection (1), as excessive to any extent;\nthe amount of the costs is to be reduced by the amount of the\nexcess.\n\n(3) An instrument under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-17a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-17a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-17a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "599cf3853910ec63db35acfa903fd2ddd00d3bcebc8a72b3a20fc2915c3d974d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-17a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17A Reduction of excessive costs",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 70,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, formulate principles or\nrules that are to be applied in determining the extent (if any) to\nwhich costs are to be treated as excessive for the purposes of\nsubsection 17(3).\n\n(2) For the purposes of the application of subsection 17(3) in relation\nto a particular claim period, if:\n\n(a) a person has incurred costs of a kind mentioned in paragraph\n17(3)(a); and\n\n(b) the costs are treated, under the principles or rules in force\nunder subsection (1), as excessive to any extent;\nthe amount of the costs is to be reduced by the amount of the\nexcess.\n\n(3) An instrument under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."
    },
