    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-18-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18 Universal service charges",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-18-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.70",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if a person is the universal service provider for\na universal service area.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            67\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Division, a universal service charge is a\ncharge imposed, or proposed to be imposed, by the person for:\n\n(a) the supply of standard telephone services to persons in the\narea; or\n\n(b) calls made from payphones in the area; or\n\n(c) the supply of prescribed carriage services to persons in the\narea.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if a person is the universal service provider for\na universal service area.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            67\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Division, a universal service charge is a\ncharge imposed, or proposed to be imposed, by the person for:\n\n(a) the supply of standard telephone services to persons in the\narea; or\n\n(b) calls made from payphones in the area; or\n\n(c) the supply of prescribed carriage services to persons in the\narea.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-18-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-18-2-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f71554dee21c9043822f822ef7e52576deff0e24cc48d588431a80e6d00da097"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-18-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18 Universal service charges",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 70,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if a person is the universal service provider for\na universal service area.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            67\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Division, a universal service charge is a\ncharge imposed, or proposed to be imposed, by the person for:\n\n(a) the supply of standard telephone services to persons in the\narea; or\n\n(b) calls made from payphones in the area; or\n\n(c) the supply of prescribed carriage services to persons in the\narea."
    },
