    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-18c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18C Content of price control determinations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-18c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.72",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A determination under section 18B relating to a universal service\ncharge may:\n\n(a) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without the\nMinister’s consent; or\n\n(b) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without the\nACCC’s consent; or\n\n(c) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without\nprior notice being given to the Minister; or\n\n(d) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without\nprior notice being given to the ACCC; or\n\n(e) empower the Minister to direct the ACCC to give the\nMinister such reports and advice as the Minister requires for\nthe purposes of assisting the Minister in deciding whether to\ngive a consent in accordance with the determination.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not, by implication, limit section 18B.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A determination under section 18B relating to a universal service\ncharge may:\n\n(a) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without the\nMinister’s consent; or\n\n(b) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without the\nACCC’s consent; or\n\n(c) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without\nprior notice being given to the Minister; or\n\n(d) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without\nprior notice being given to the ACCC; or\n\n(e) empower the Minister to direct the ACCC to give the\nMinister such reports and advice as the Minister requires for\nthe purposes of assisting the Minister in deciding whether to\ngive a consent in accordance with the determination.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not, by implication, limit section 18B.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-18c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-18c-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4c670470acc069993312ef94a1b9cf30220fd63616055ece9de6b54bec74b7c7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-18c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18C Content of price control determinations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 72,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A determination under section 18B relating to a universal service\ncharge may:\n\n(a) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without the\nMinister’s consent; or\n\n(b) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without the\nACCC’s consent; or\n\n(c) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without\nprior notice being given to the Minister; or\n\n(d) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without\nprior notice being given to the ACCC; or\n\n(e) empower the Minister to direct the ACCC to give the\nMinister such reports and advice as the Minister requires for\nthe purposes of assisting the Minister in deciding whether to\ngive a consent in accordance with the determination.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not, by implication, limit section 18B."
    },
