      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.72",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A determination under section 18B relating to a universal service\ncharge may:\n\n(a) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without the\nMinister’s consent; or\n\n(b) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without the\nACCC’s consent; or\n\n(c) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without\nprior notice being given to the Minister; or\n\n(d) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without\nprior notice being given to the ACCC; or\n\n(e) empower the Minister to direct the ACCC to give the\nMinister such reports and advice as the Minister requires for\nthe purposes of assisting the Minister in deciding whether to\ngive a consent in accordance with the determination.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A determination under section 18B relating to a universal service\ncharge may:\n\n(a) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without the\nMinister’s consent; or\n\n(b) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without the\nACCC’s consent; or\n\n(c) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without\nprior notice being given to the Minister; or\n\n(d) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without\nprior notice being given to the ACCC; or\n\n(e) empower the Minister to direct the ACCC to give the\nMinister such reports and advice as the Minister requires for\nthe purposes of assisting the Minister in deciding whether to\ngive a consent in accordance with the determination.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-18c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-18c-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-18c-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ef49c1c54952441d05439934962a15d56bf237e945bf9499d4499e3651ddee07",
      "skos:note": "Prohibit charge imposition or alteration without consent."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-18c-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18C(1) Content of price control determinations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 72,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A determination under section 18B relating to a universal service\ncharge may:\n\n(a) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without the\nMinister’s consent; or\n\n(b) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without the\nACCC’s consent; or\n\n(c) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without\nprior notice being given to the Minister; or\n\n(d) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without\nprior notice being given to the ACCC; or\n\n(e) empower the Minister to direct the ACCC to give the\nMinister such reports and advice as the Minister requires for\nthe purposes of assisting the Minister in deciding whether to\ngive a consent in accordance with the determination."
    },
