    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20F ACA to assess eligible revenue",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACA must make a written assessment of each participating\nperson’s eligible revenue for an eligible revenue period.\nNote:\nThe assessment may be included in the same document as any other\nassessment the ACA makes under this Part (see section 20Y).\n\n(2) A person’s eligible revenue:\n\n(a) must be assessed as zero if the person’s eligible revenue is\nless than the amount (the threshold amount) determined in\nwriting by the Minister for the purposes of this subsection; or\n\n(b) in any other case—must be reduced by the threshold amount.\n\n(3) Subject to section 20G and subsection (2), the assessment must be\nbased on:\n\n(a) the person’s eligible revenue return; and\n\n(b) the information and documents obtained by the ACA because\nof its inquiries into the correctness of the return; and\n\n(c) any other information or documents that the ACA has and\nthat it thinks relevant to making the assessment.\n\n(4) A determination made for the purposes of subsection (2) is a\ndisallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n(5) The ACA must give a copy of an assessment of a person’s eligible\nrevenue to the person concerned.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACA must make a written assessment of each participating\nperson’s eligible revenue for an eligible revenue period.\nNote:\nThe assessment may be included in the same document as any other\nassessment the ACA makes under this Part (see section 20Y).\n\n(2) A person’s eligible revenue:\n\n(a) must be assessed as zero if the person’s eligible revenue is\nless than the amount (the threshold amount) determined in\nwriting by the Minister for the purposes of this subsection; or\n\n(b) in any other case—must be reduced by the threshold amount.\n\n(3) Subject to section 20G and subsection (2), the assessment must be\nbased on:\n\n(a) the person’s eligible revenue return; and\n\n(b) the information and documents obtained by the ACA because\nof its inquiries into the correctness of the return; and\n\n(c) any other information or documents that the ACA has and\nthat it thinks relevant to making the assessment.\n\n(4) A determination made for the purposes of subsection (2) is a\ndisallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n(5) The ACA must give a copy of an assessment of a person’s eligible\nrevenue to the person concerned.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20f-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20f-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20f-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a3c25788e6ce46f3c2aa7916aa7c80bc0f6da3ea8924921e6620fee44f3bdd6f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20F ACA to assess eligible revenue",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACA must make a written assessment of each participating\nperson’s eligible revenue for an eligible revenue period.\nNote:\nThe assessment may be included in the same document as any other\nassessment the ACA makes under this Part (see section 20Y).\n\n(2) A person’s eligible revenue:\n\n(a) must be assessed as zero if the person’s eligible revenue is\nless than the amount (the threshold amount) determined in\nwriting by the Minister for the purposes of this subsection; or\n\n(b) in any other case—must be reduced by the threshold amount.\n\n(3) Subject to section 20G and subsection (2), the assessment must be\nbased on:\n\n(a) the person’s eligible revenue return; and\n\n(b) the information and documents obtained by the ACA because\nof its inquiries into the correctness of the return; and\n\n(c) any other information or documents that the ACA has and\nthat it thinks relevant to making the assessment.\n\n(4) A determination made for the purposes of subsection (2) is a\ndisallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n(5) The ACA must give a copy of an assessment of a person’s eligible\nrevenue to the person concerned."
    },
