    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20G Assessment based on estimate of eligible revenue",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a participating person fails to give the ACA an eligible revenue\nreturn for an eligible revenue period, the ACA may:\n\n(a) estimate the person’s eligible revenue for that period; and\n\n(b) make a written assessment under section 20F of the person’s\neligible revenue for that period based on that estimate (but\ntaking into account subsection 20F(2)).\n\n(2) The ACA must give at least 14 days’ notice to the person of the\nACA’s proposal to make the assessment based on the estimate, and\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            75\nof the amount of eligible return proposed to be assessed. The notice\nmust be in writing.\n\n(3) The ACA must not make an assessment based on an estimate after\nreceiving an eligible revenue return for the period from the person\nconcerned.\n\n(4) However, if the ACA has made an assessment based on the\nestimate, the ACA is not required to change it if an eligible\nrevenue return is later given to the ACA.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a participating person fails to give the ACA an eligible revenue\nreturn for an eligible revenue period, the ACA may:\n\n(a) estimate the person’s eligible revenue for that period; and\n\n(b) make a written assessment under section 20F of the person’s\neligible revenue for that period based on that estimate (but\ntaking into account subsection 20F(2)).\n\n(2) The ACA must give at least 14 days’ notice to the person of the\nACA’s proposal to make the assessment based on the estimate, and\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            75\nof the amount of eligible return proposed to be assessed. The notice\nmust be in writing.\n\n(3) The ACA must not make an assessment based on an estimate after\nreceiving an eligible revenue return for the period from the person\nconcerned.\n\n(4) However, if the ACA has made an assessment based on the\nestimate, the ACA is not required to change it if an eligible\nrevenue return is later given to the ACA.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20g-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20g-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20g-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "38e9d4902cd278af5b5368872552f028f1afeea01f20bbda446373776d0b1819"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20G Assessment based on estimate of eligible revenue",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a participating person fails to give the ACA an eligible revenue\nreturn for an eligible revenue period, the ACA may:\n\n(a) estimate the person’s eligible revenue for that period; and\n\n(b) make a written assessment under section 20F of the person’s\neligible revenue for that period based on that estimate (but\ntaking into account subsection 20F(2)).\n\n(2) The ACA must give at least 14 days’ notice to the person of the\nACA’s proposal to make the assessment based on the estimate, and\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            75\nof the amount of eligible return proposed to be assessed. The notice\nmust be in writing.\n\n(3) The ACA must not make an assessment based on an estimate after\nreceiving an eligible revenue return for the period from the person\nconcerned.\n\n(4) However, if the ACA has made an assessment based on the\nestimate, the ACA is not required to change it if an eligible\nrevenue return is later given to the ACA."
    },
