    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20H Levy contribution factor",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.79",
      "values:originalText": "(1) After the ACA has assessed the eligible revenue of participating\npersons for an eligible revenue period, the ACA must work out a\nlevy contribution factor for the period for each of those persons.\nNote:\nThe levy contribution factor is used to work out the levy debit of a\nparticipating person. See section 20R.\n\n(2) The levy contribution factor for an eligible revenue period is the\namount worked out using the following formula:\nIndividual eligible revenue\nTotal eligible revenue\n\nwhere:\nindividual eligible revenue means the assessed eligible revenue of\nthe participating person for the eligible revenue period.\ntotal eligible revenue means the total assessed eligible revenue for\nthe eligible revenue period of all the participating persons for the\nperiod.\nSubdivision B—Levy credits",
      "skos:definition": "(1) After the ACA has assessed the eligible revenue of participating\npersons for an eligible revenue period, the ACA must work out a\nlevy contribution factor for the period for each of those persons.\nNote:\nThe levy contribution factor is used to work out the levy debit of a\nparticipating person. See section 20R.\n\n(2) The levy contribution factor for an eligible revenue period is the\namount worked out using the following formula:\nIndividual eligible revenue\nTotal eligible revenue\n\nwhere:\nindividual eligible revenue means the assessed eligible revenue of\nthe participating person for the eligible revenue period.\ntotal eligible revenue means the total assessed eligible revenue for\nthe eligible revenue period of all the participating persons for the\nperiod.\nSubdivision B—Levy credits",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20h-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f2b15745274bba19fbde14a5b66df0f67336dae96d5244c9543e4d34f753e016"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
