    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20k",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20K Audit report of claim",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20k"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A claim must be accompanied by a report of an approved auditor\nthat:\n\n(a) is in a form approved in writing by the ACA; and\n\n(b) states that the auditor has audited the claim; and\n\n(c) contains a determination, in the terms specified in the form,\nof the auditor’s opinion; and\n\n(d) states that the auditor has been given sufficient information\nand assistance in order to audit the claim; and\n\n(e) includes all other statements and information required by the\nform to be included.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            77\n\n(2) However, the Minister may, by making a written determination,\nmodify the requirements in subsection (1), including by omitting,\nadding or substituting requirements.\n\n(3) This section does not apply to a person if the ACA gives written\nnotice to the person to that effect.\n\n(4) A copy of a determination under subsection (2) must be published\nin the Gazette.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A claim must be accompanied by a report of an approved auditor\nthat:\n\n(a) is in a form approved in writing by the ACA; and\n\n(b) states that the auditor has audited the claim; and\n\n(c) contains a determination, in the terms specified in the form,\nof the auditor’s opinion; and\n\n(d) states that the auditor has been given sufficient information\nand assistance in order to audit the claim; and\n\n(e) includes all other statements and information required by the\nform to be included.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            77\n\n(2) However, the Minister may, by making a written determination,\nmodify the requirements in subsection (1), including by omitting,\nadding or substituting requirements.\n\n(3) This section does not apply to a person if the ACA gives written\nnotice to the person to that effect.\n\n(4) A copy of a determination under subsection (2) must be published\nin the Gazette.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20k-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20k-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20k-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20k-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d5d2e543138e510f703f7c396dd2093d7abe29bcd20bc352e3f822d5a59c7373"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20k",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20K Audit report of claim",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A claim must be accompanied by a report of an approved auditor\nthat:\n\n(a) is in a form approved in writing by the ACA; and\n\n(b) states that the auditor has audited the claim; and\n\n(c) contains a determination, in the terms specified in the form,\nof the auditor’s opinion; and\n\n(d) states that the auditor has been given sufficient information\nand assistance in order to audit the claim; and\n\n(e) includes all other statements and information required by the\nform to be included.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            77\n\n(2) However, the Minister may, by making a written determination,\nmodify the requirements in subsection (1), including by omitting,\nadding or substituting requirements.\n\n(3) This section does not apply to a person if the ACA gives written\nnotice to the person to that effect.\n\n(4) A copy of a determination under subsection (2) must be published\nin the Gazette."
    },
