    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20P Principles for assessing and adjusting claims",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.82",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may determine in writing principles that are to be\napplied in assessing (including adjusting) claims for a levy credit.\nThe principles apply from the date specified in the determination.\n\n(2) Before making the determination, the Minister must invite all\naffected carriers and carrier service providers to make submissions\nwithin a specified period to the Minister about the proposed\nprinciples. The period specified must be reasonable.\n\n(3) The ACA must apply the principles (if any) made by the Minister\nunder this section in making assessments under this Part.\n\n(4) A determination under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument\nfor the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            79\nSubdivision C—Entitlement to levy distributions and liability\nfor levy\n20Q  No levy payable unless at least one claim for a levy credit is\nmade\n\nIf no claim for a levy credit for a claim period has been made under\nsection 20J within the period for making such claims, no person is\nliable to pay an amount of levy in respect of that period.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may determine in writing principles that are to be\napplied in assessing (including adjusting) claims for a levy credit.\nThe principles apply from the date specified in the determination.\n\n(2) Before making the determination, the Minister must invite all\naffected carriers and carrier service providers to make submissions\nwithin a specified period to the Minister about the proposed\nprinciples. The period specified must be reasonable.\n\n(3) The ACA must apply the principles (if any) made by the Minister\nunder this section in making assessments under this Part.\n\n(4) A determination under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument\nfor the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            79\nSubdivision C—Entitlement to levy distributions and liability\nfor levy\n20Q  No levy payable unless at least one claim for a levy credit is\nmade\n\nIf no claim for a levy credit for a claim period has been made under\nsection 20J within the period for making such claims, no person is\nliable to pay an amount of levy in respect of that period.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20p-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20p-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20p-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20p-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e20939e1e4727985e698d51ec69c30180e1866791183cf7500a4c4799323816f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20P Principles for assessing and adjusting claims",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 82,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may determine in writing principles that are to be\napplied in assessing (including adjusting) claims for a levy credit.\nThe principles apply from the date specified in the determination.\n\n(2) Before making the determination, the Minister must invite all\naffected carriers and carrier service providers to make submissions\nwithin a specified period to the Minister about the proposed\nprinciples. The period specified must be reasonable.\n\n(3) The ACA must apply the principles (if any) made by the Minister\nunder this section in making assessments under this Part.\n\n(4) A determination under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument\nfor the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            79\nSubdivision C—Entitlement to levy distributions and liability\nfor levy\n20Q  No levy payable unless at least one claim for a levy credit is\nmade\n\nIf no claim for a levy credit for a claim period has been made under\nsection 20J within the period for making such claims, no person is\nliable to pay an amount of levy in respect of that period."
    },
    {
