    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20p-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20P(4) Principles for assessing and adjusting claims",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20p-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.82",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A determination under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument\nfor the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            79\nSubdivision C—Entitlement to levy distributions and liability\nfor levy\n20Q  No levy payable unless at least one claim for a levy credit is\nmade\n\nIf no claim for a levy credit for a claim period has been made under\nsection 20J within the period for making such claims, no person is\nliable to pay an amount of levy in respect of that period.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A determination under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument\nfor the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            79\nSubdivision C—Entitlement to levy distributions and liability\nfor levy\n20Q  No levy payable unless at least one claim for a levy credit is\nmade\n\nIf no claim for a levy credit for a claim period has been made under\nsection 20J within the period for making such claims, no person is\nliable to pay an amount of levy in respect of that period.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20p"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20p-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20p-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ba4deb753b81567cf1e722aa0fa352972116b1dafb17160968b33365ca2f15a9",
      "skos:note": "No levy payable unless at least one claim for a levy credit is made."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20p-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20P(4) Principles for assessing and adjusting claims",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 82,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A determination under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument\nfor the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            79\nSubdivision C—Entitlement to levy distributions and liability\nfor levy\n20Q  No levy payable unless at least one claim for a levy credit is\nmade\n\nIf no claim for a levy credit for a claim period has been made under\nsection 20J within the period for making such claims, no person is\nliable to pay an amount of levy in respect of that period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20p-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20p-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20p-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits payment of levy unless claim for credit is made.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20r",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20R Levy debit of a participating person",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20r"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.83",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For each claim period, the ACA must work out a levy debit for\neach participating person for the last eligible revenue period that\nended before the start of the claim period.\n\n(2) The levy debit is the amount worked out using the formula:\nLevy contribution factor\nTotal levy credits\n×\n\nwhere:\nlevy contribution factor means the person’s levy contribution\nfactor for that eligible revenue period worked out under\nsection 20H.\ntotal levy credits means the total of all the levy credits to which\npersons are entitled for that claim period.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by written determination, modify the formula in\nsubsection (2).\nNote:\nThe Minister may, for example, increase the amount of total levy\ncredits to take account of the possibility of defaults in the payment of\nlevy for a claim period.\n\n(4) A determination under subsection (3) is a disallowable instrument\nfor the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For each claim period, the ACA must work out a levy debit for\neach participating person for the last eligible revenue period that\nended before the start of the claim period.\n\n(2) The levy debit is the amount worked out using the formula:\nLevy contribution factor\nTotal levy credits\n×\n\nwhere:\nlevy contribution factor means the person’s levy contribution\nfactor for that eligible revenue period worked out under\nsection 20H.\ntotal levy credits means the total of all the levy credits to which\npersons are entitled for that claim period.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by written determination, modify the formula in\nsubsection (2).\nNote:\nThe Minister may, for example, increase the amount of total levy\ncredits to take account of the possibility of defaults in the payment of\nlevy for a claim period.\n\n(4) A determination under subsection (3) is a disallowable instrument\nfor the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20r-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20r-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20r-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20r-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d9afecd71548f6b2abe04f8b91426f9250b105dd61230b45f0f7710298c1a9ff"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20r",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20R Levy debit of a participating person",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 83,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For each claim period, the ACA must work out a levy debit for\neach participating person for the last eligible revenue period that\nended before the start of the claim period.\n\n(2) The levy debit is the amount worked out using the formula:\nLevy contribution factor\nTotal levy credits\n×\n\nwhere:\nlevy contribution factor means the person’s levy contribution\nfactor for that eligible revenue period worked out under\nsection 20H.\ntotal levy credits means the total of all the levy credits to which\npersons are entitled for that claim period.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by written determination, modify the formula in\nsubsection (2).\nNote:\nThe Minister may, for example, increase the amount of total levy\ncredits to take account of the possibility of defaults in the payment of\nlevy for a claim period.\n\n(4) A determination under subsection (3) is a disallowable instrument\nfor the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."
    },
