    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20u",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20U ACA to make written assessment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20u"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For each claim period, the ACA must make a written assessment\nsetting out:\n\n(a) the matters in subsections (2), (3) and (4); and\n\n(b) the total of all levy credits to which persons are entitled for\nthe claim period.\n\n(2) For each participating person for the last eligible revenue period\nthat ended before the start of the claim period, the assessment must\nset out:\n\n(a) the person’s levy debit under section 20R for the claim\nperiod; and\n\n(b) the person’s levy debit balance (if any) under section 20S for\nthe claim period; and\n\n(c) if the person has a levy debit balance—the levy payable by\nthe person on that balance.\nNote:\nSection 20Z sets out when the levy is payable.\n\n(3) For each universal service provider for the claim period, the\nassessment must set out:\n\n(a) the universal service subsidy to which the ACA assesses the\nprovider is entitled for the claim period; and\n\n(b) the provider’s levy credit balance (if any) under section 20T\nfor the claim period; and\n\n(c) if the provider has a levy credit balance—the amount payable\nto the provider under section 21C for the claim period.\n\n(4) For each digital data service provider for the claim period, the\nassessment must set out:\n\n(a) the provider’s digital data cost for the claim period; and\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            81\n\n(b) the provider’s levy credit balance (if any) under section 20T\nfor the claim period; and\n\n(c) if the provider has a levy credit balance—the amount payable\nto the provider under section 21C for the claim period.\n\n(5) The assessment must be made on the basis of:\n\n(a) the assessments under section 20N of levy credits for the\nclaim period; and\n\n(b) the assessments under section 20F of eligible revenue for\neach participating person for the last eligible revenue period\nthat ended before the start of the claim period; and\n\n(c) any other information or documents that the ACA has and\nthat it thinks relevant to making the assessment.\n\n(6) The ACA must act expeditiously in preparing its assessment.\nHowever, a failure to comply with this subsection does not affect\nthe validity of the assessment.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For each claim period, the ACA must make a written assessment\nsetting out:\n\n(a) the matters in subsections (2), (3) and (4); and\n\n(b) the total of all levy credits to which persons are entitled for\nthe claim period.\n\n(2) For each participating person for the last eligible revenue period\nthat ended before the start of the claim period, the assessment must\nset out:\n\n(a) the person’s levy debit under section 20R for the claim\nperiod; and\n\n(b) the person’s levy debit balance (if any) under section 20S for\nthe claim period; and\n\n(c) if the person has a levy debit balance—the levy payable by\nthe person on that balance.\nNote:\nSection 20Z sets out when the levy is payable.\n\n(3) For each universal service provider for the claim period, the\nassessment must set out:\n\n(a) the universal service subsidy to which the ACA assesses the\nprovider is entitled for the claim period; and\n\n(b) the provider’s levy credit balance (if any) under section 20T\nfor the claim period; and\n\n(c) if the provider has a levy credit balance—the amount payable\nto the provider under section 21C for the claim period.\n\n(4) For each digital data service provider for the claim period, the\nassessment must set out:\n\n(a) the provider’s digital data cost for the claim period; and\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            81\n\n(b) the provider’s levy credit balance (if any) under section 20T\nfor the claim period; and\n\n(c) if the provider has a levy credit balance—the amount payable\nto the provider under section 21C for the claim period.\n\n(5) The assessment must be made on the basis of:\n\n(a) the assessments under section 20N of levy credits for the\nclaim period; and\n\n(b) the assessments under section 20F of eligible revenue for\neach participating person for the last eligible revenue period\nthat ended before the start of the claim period; a",
      "cml:hasPart": [
