        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20u-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c0a410dd52c66e6e0dc914996b2a68e11f427a63f8d276cc19a93ad65f09fd85",
      "skos:note": "Digital data service provider must provide written assessment with specific details.",
      "dc:description": "True"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-20u-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20U(4) ACA to make written assessment",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "(4) For each digital data service provider for the claim period, the\nassessment must set out:\n\n(a) the provider’s digital data cost for the claim period; and\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            81\n\n(b) the provider’s levy credit balance (if any) under section 20T\nfor the claim period; and\n\n(c) if the provider has a levy credit balance—the amount payable\nto the provider under section 21C for the claim period."
    },
