    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 Universal Service Account",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-21"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.88",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Universal Service Account that was, immediately before the\ncommencement of this section, in existence because of section 82\nof the unamended Act continues in existence under and subject to\nthe provisions of this Act.\n\n(2) The Universal Service Account is a Special Account within the\nmeaning of the FMA Act.\n\n(3) The Universal Service Account is to be administered by:\n\n(a) the Department; or\n\n(b) the ACA, if the ACA is a prescribed Agency within the\nmeaning of the FMA Act.\n\n(4) If there is a change to who is to administer the Universal Service\nAccount in accordance with subsection (3), the Minister may\ndetermine in writing arrangements to deal with any issues of a\ntransitional nature that may arise as a result of the change.\n\n(5) A copy of a determination under subsection (4) must be published\nin the Gazette.\n\n(6) In this section:\nFMA Act means the Financial Management and Accountability\nAct 1997.\nunamended Act means this Act as in force immediately before the\ncommencement of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications\n(Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act\n(No. 2) 2000.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Universal Service Account that was, immediately before the\ncommencement of this section, in existence because of section 82\nof the unamended Act continues in existence under and subject to\nthe provisions of this Act.\n\n(2) The Universal Service Account is a Special Account within the\nmeaning of the FMA Act.\n\n(3) The Universal Service Account is to be administered by:\n\n(a) the Department; or\n\n(b) the ACA, if the ACA is a prescribed Agency within the\nmeaning of the FMA Act.\n\n(4) If there is a change to who is to administer the Universal Service\nAccount in accordance with subsection (3), the Minister may\ndetermine in writing arrangements to deal with any issues of a\ntransitional nature that may arise as a result of the change.\n\n(5) A copy of a determination under subsection (4) must be published\nin the Gazette.\n\n(6) In this section:\nFMA Act means the Financial Management and Accountability\nAct 1997.\nunamended Act means this Act as in force immediately before the\ncommencement of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications\n(Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act\n(No. 2) 2000.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "954afd73677ccd755b45beac2d670d9aa4e00e6a875372a2851e3240b485469c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-21",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 Universal Service Account",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 88,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Universal Service Account that was, immediately before the\ncommencement of this section, in existence because of section 82\nof the unamended Act continues in existence under and subject to\nthe provisions of this Act.\n\n(2) The Universal Service Account is a Special Account within the\nmeaning of the FMA Act.\n\n(3) The Universal Service Account is to be administered by:\n\n(a) the Department; or\n\n(b) the ACA, if the ACA is a prescribed Agency within the\nmeaning of the FMA Act.\n\n(4) If there is a change to who is to administer the Universal Service\nAccount in accordance with subsection (3), the Minister may\ndetermine in writing arrangements to deal with any issues of a\ntransitional nature that may arise as a result of the change.\n\n(5) A copy of a determination under subsection (4) must be published\nin the Gazette.\n\n(6) In this section:\nFMA Act means the Financial Management and Accountability\nAct 1997.\nunamended Act means this Act as in force immediately before the\ncommencement of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications\n(Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act\n(No. 2) 2000."
    },
