        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21B Purposes of Universal Service Account",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-21b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.89",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Amounts standing to the credit of the Universal Service Account\nmay be expended:\n\n(a) in payment of any amounts payable under section 21C; and\n\n(b) in payment of any refunds under section 20ZE; and\n\n(c) in refunding any amounts paid into the Universal Service\nAccount in error; and\n\n(d) in making distributions in accordance with section 21D; and\n\n(e) in reimbursing the Commonwealth for:\n\n(i) the costs or expenses incurred by the Commonwealth or\nthe ACA in administering the Telecommunications\n(Universal Service Levy) Act 1997 and this Division\nduring any period; and\n\n(ii) without limiting subparagraph (i), costs or expenses\nincurred in connection with recovering levy; and\n\n(iii) costs incurred by the Commonwealth during the period\nin collecting, compiling, analysing and publishing\ninformation about the operation of that Act and this\nDivision.\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(e), the Minister administering\nthe Financial Management and Accountability Act 1997 may, from\ntime to time, determine the amount of a reimbursement to be made\nto the Commonwealth in relation to a period on such basis as he or\nshe thinks appropriate.\n\n(3) Despite subsection (2), the total of the amounts reimbursed under\nparagraph (1)(e) must not exceed the total of the amounts paid into\nthe Universal Service Account under paragraph 21A(b) (including\nany interest earned on those amounts).\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Amounts standing to the credit of the Universal Service Account\nmay be expended:\n\n(a) in payment of any amounts payable under section 21C; and\n\n(b) in payment of any refunds under section 20ZE; and\n\n(c) in refunding any amounts paid into the Universal Service\nAccount in error; and\n\n(d) in making distributions in accordance with section 21D; and\n\n(e) in reimbursing the Commonwealth for:\n\n(i) the costs or expenses incurred by the Commonwealth or\nthe ACA in administering the Telecommunications\n(Universal Service Levy) Act 1997 and this Division\nduring any period; and\n\n(ii) without limiting subparagraph (i), costs or expenses\nincurred in connection with recovering levy; and\n\n(iii) costs incurred by the Commonwealth during the period\nin collecting, compiling, analysing and publishing\ninformation about the operation of that Act and this\nDivision.\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(e), the Minister administering\nthe Financial Management and Accountability Act 1997 may, from\ntime to time, determine the amount of a reimbursement to be made\nto the Commonwealth in relation to a period on such basis as he or\nshe thinks appropriate.\n\n(3) Despite subsection (2), the total of the amounts reimbursed under\nparagraph (1)(e) must not exceed the total of the amounts paid into\nthe Universal Service Account under paragraph 21A(b) (including\nany interest earned on those amounts).\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1ad259f9b504b8634ea30ba12ea6d6db22d8bf1239eb0f6ee1c92f40b36ca552"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-21b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21B Purposes of Universal Service Account",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 89,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Amounts standing to the credit of the Universal Service Account\nmay be expended:\n\n(a) in payment of any amounts payable under section 21C; and\n\n(b) in payment of any refunds under section 20ZE; and\n\n(c) in refunding any amounts paid into the Universal Service\nAccount in error; and\n\n(d) in making distributions in accordance with section 21D; and\n\n(e) in reimbursing the Commonwealth for:\n\n(i) the costs or expenses incurred by the Commonwealth or\nthe ACA in administering the Telecommunications\n(Universal Service Levy) Act 1997 and this Division\nduring any period; and\n\n(ii) without limiting subparagraph (i), costs or expenses\nincurred in connection with recovering levy; and\n\n(iii) costs incurred by the Commonwealth during the period\nin collecting, compiling, analysing and publishing\ninformation about the operation of that Act and this\nDivision.\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(e), the Minister administering\nthe Financial Management and Accountability Act 1997 may, from\ntime to time, determine the amount of a reimbursement to be made\nto the Commonwealth in relation to a period on such basis as he or\nshe thinks appropriate.\n\n(3) Despite subsection (2), the total of the amounts reimbursed under\nparagraph (1)(e) must not exceed the total of the amounts paid into\nthe Universal Service Account under paragraph 21A(b) (including\nany interest earned on those amounts).\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21b-ss-1",
