    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21D Distribution of remaining balance of the Universal Service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-21d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "Account\n\n(1) The ACA may distribute to persons who are or were participating\npersons any balance of the Universal Service Account that remains\nafter all amounts payable out of it for a claim period have been\npaid.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            87\n\n(2) The Minister may determine in writing rules for making those\ndistributions. The ACA must comply with those rules.\n\n(3) A determination under subsection (2) is a disallowable instrument\nfor the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "Account\n\n(1) The ACA may distribute to persons who are or were participating\npersons any balance of the Universal Service Account that remains\nafter all amounts payable out of it for a claim period have been\npaid.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            87\n\n(2) The Minister may determine in writing rules for making those\ndistributions. The ACA must comply with those rules.\n\n(3) A determination under subsection (2) is a disallowable instrument\nfor the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21d-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7e1b0d5641f2640ce9a953ec231eea2c27a2a7633f7d3c273e5735e2b30c10b7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-21d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21D Distribution of remaining balance of the Universal Service",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "Account\n\n(1) The ACA may distribute to persons who are or were participating\npersons any balance of the Universal Service Account that remains\nafter all amounts payable out of it for a claim period have been\npaid.\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            87\n\n(2) The Minister may determine in writing rules for making those\ndistributions. The ACA must comply with those rules.\n\n(3) A determination under subsection (2) is a disallowable instrument\nfor the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."
    },
