        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "40c58b3044b96a5d9a640cc9aceebe7cd9bd2670c93ace4159de2592e4bf18dc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-22d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22D Minister may modify way in which this Division applies",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 94,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may determine in writing that this Division applies to\ninformation subject to such modifications as are specified in the\ndetermination.\n\n(2) A determination under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument\nfor the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n(3) In this section:\n\nNew Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards)\nAct 1999  Schedule 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            91\nmodifications includes omissions, additions and substitutions."
