    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-23",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23 ACA must maintain Register/s",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-23"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.95",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACA is to maintain a Register or Registers in which the ACA\nincludes a copy of each of the following documents (indicating\nwhether the document is currently in force):\n\n(a) a determination made under section 11C, (contestable service\nobligations);\n\n(b) a determination made under section 14 (alternative\narrangements for fulfilling the universal service obligation);\n\n(c) an approved policy statement for a primary universal service\nprovider or a competing universal service provider;\n\n(d) an approved standard marketing plan for a primary universal\nservice provider or a competing universal service provider;\n\n(e) an approved ATS marketing plan for a primary universal\nservice provider or a competing universal service provider;\n\n(f) an approved digital data service plan for a digital data service\nprovider.\n\n(2) The Register or Registers may be maintained by electronic means.\n\n(3) A person may, on payment of the charge (if any) fixed by a\ndetermination under section 53 of the Australian Communications\nAuthority Act 1997:\n\n(a) inspect the Register or Registers; and\n\n(b) make a copy of, or take extracts from, the Register or\nRegisters.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, if a Register is maintained by\nelectronic means, a person is taken to have made a copy of, or\ntaken an extract from, the Register if the ACA gives the person a\nprintout of some or all of the Register.\n\n(5) If a person requests that a copy be provided in an electronic form,\nthe ACA may provide the relevant information:\n\n(a) on a data processing device; or\n\n(b) by way of electronic transmission.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACA is to maintain a Register or Registers in which the ACA\nincludes a copy of each of the following documents (indicating\nwhether the document is currently in force):\n\n(a) a determination made under section 11C, (contestable service\nobligations);\n\n(b) a determination made under section 14 (alternative\narrangements for fulfilling the universal service obligation);\n\n(c) an approved policy statement for a primary universal service\nprovider or a competing universal service provider;\n\n(d) an approved standard marketing plan for a primary universal\nservice provider or a competing universal service provider;\n\n(e) an approved ATS marketing plan for a primary universal\nservice provider or a competing universal service provider;\n\n(f) an approved digital data service plan for a digital data service\nprovider.\n\n(2) The Register or Registers may be maintained by electronic means.\n\n(3) A person may, on payment of the charge (if any) fixed by a\ndetermination under section 53 of the Australian Communications\nAuthority Act 1997:\n\n(a) inspect the Register or Registers; and\n\n(b) make a copy of, or take extracts from, the Register or\nRegisters.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, if a Register is maintained by\nelectronic means, a person is taken to have made a copy of, or\ntaken an extract from, the Register if the ACA gives the person a\nprintout of some or all of the Register.\n\n(5) If a person requests that a copy be provided in an electronic form,\nthe ACA may provide the relevant information:\n\n(a) on a data processing device; or\n\n(b) by way of electronic transmission.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-23-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-23-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-23-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-23-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-23-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c8b2df46b137868894cb2e80ed6df059776b99fd975a493ca6fb94ac32829c09"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-23",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23 ACA must maintain Register/s",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 95,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACA is to maintain a Register or Registers in which the ACA\nincludes a copy of each of the following documents (indicating\nwhether the document is currently in force):\n\n(a) a determination made under section 11C, (contestable service\nobligations);\n\n(b) a determination made under section 14 (alternative\narrangements for fulfilling the universal service obligation);\n\n(c) an approved policy statement for a primary universal service\nprovider or a competing universal service provider;\n\n(d) an approved standard marketing plan for a primary universal\nservice provider or a competing universal service provider;\n\n(e) an approved ATS marketing plan for a primary universal\nservice provider or a competing universal service provider;\n\n(f) an approved digital data service plan for a digital data service\nprovider.\n\n(2) The Register or Registers may be maintained by electronic means.\n\n(3) A person may, on payment of the charge (if any) fixed by a\ndetermination under section 53 of the Australian Communications\nAuthority Act 1997:\n\n(a) inspect the Register or Registers; and\n\n(b) make a copy of, or take extracts from, the Register or\nRegisters.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, if a Register is maintained by\nelectronic means, a person is taken to have made a copy of, or\ntaken an extract from, the Register if the ACA gives the person a\nprintout of some or all of the Register.\n\n(5) If a person requests that a copy be provided in an electronic form,\nthe ACA may provide the relevant information:\n\n(a) on a data processing device; or\n\n(b) by way of electronic transmission.\n\nSchedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999"
    },
