      "cml:conclusionText": "(B)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-2-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Effect of instruments made under repealed Part 2",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-2-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.98",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nFor the purposes of this item, an eligible instrument means regulations,\na declaration, a determination, a direction, a notice or any other\ninstrument that was:\n\n(a) made or given under a provision (the original provision) of\nPart 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and\nService Standards) Act 1999 in the table in subitem (3), or\nmade or given for the purposes of such a provision; and\n\nApplication and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            95\n\n(b) in force immediately before this Act received the Royal\nAssent.\n(2)\nDespite the repeal and substitution of that Part by Schedule 1 to this\nAct, an eligible instrument has effect, after that Schedule commences,\nas if:\n\n(a) it had been made or given under, or for the purposes of, the\nequivalent provision of that Part in the table in subitem (3);\nand\n\n(b) any requirement for the making or giving of the eligible\ninstrument had been satisfied.\n(3)\nThis table sets out the original provisions, and their equivalent\nprovisions, of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999.\n\nEquivalent provisions of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999\nItem\nThis original provision\n(before this Act receives the\nRoyal Assent):\n... is equivalent, after Schedule 1\ncommences, to this provision:\nsubparagraph 11(b)(iii)\nsubparagraph 9C(b)(iii)\nsection 12\nsection 9D\nsection 13\nsection 9E\nsection 14\nsection 9F\nsubsection 14A(1)\nsubsection 10F(1)\nsubsection 14A(5)\nsubsection 10G(1)\nsection 17\nsubsection 20B(1)\nsection 18\nsection 8F\nsubsection 19(3)\nsubsection 9(3)\nsubsection 19(5)\nsubsection 9A(2)\nsubsection 19A(8)\nsubsection 10D(1)\nsubsection 19B(1)\nsubsection 10H(1)\nsubsection 19C(1)\nsubsection 10J(1)\nsection 26A\nsection 15\nsubsection 38(2)\nsubsection 12Y(2)\nsubsection 40G(1)\nsubsection 15J(1)\n\nSchedule 2  Application and transitional provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nFor the purposes of this item, an eligible instrument means regulations,\na declaration, a determination, a direction, a notice or any other\ninstrument that was:\n\n(a) made or given under a provision (the original provision) of\nPart 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and\nService Standards) Act 1999 in the table in subitem (3), or\nmade or given for the purposes of such a provision; and\n\nApplication and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            95\n\n(b) in force immediately before this Act received the Royal\nAssent.\n(2)\nDespite the repeal and substitution of that Part by Schedule 1 to this\nAct, an eligible instrument has effect, after that Schedule commences,\nas if:\n\n(a) it had been made or given under, or for the purposes of, the\nequivalent provision of that Part in the table in subitem (3);\nand\n\n(b) any requirement for the making or giving of the eligible\ninstrument had been satisfied.\n(3)\nThis table sets out the original provisions, and their equivalent\nprovisions, of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999.\n\nEquivalent provisions of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999\nItem\nThis original provision\n(before this Act receives the\nRoyal Assent):\n... is equivalent, after Schedule 1\ncommences, to this provision:\nsubparagraph 11(b)(iii)\nsubparagraph 9C(b)(iii)\nsection 12\nsection 9D\nsection 13\nsection 9E\nsection 14\nsection 9F\nsubsection 14A(1)\nsubsection 10F(1)\nsubsection 14A(5)\nsubsection 10G(1)\nsection 17\nsubsection 20B(1)\nsection 18\nsection 8F\nsubsection 19(3)\nsubsection 9(3)\nsubsection 19(5)\nsubsection 9A(2)\nsubsection 19A(8)\nsubsection 10D(1)\nsubsection 19B(1)\nsubsection 10H(1)\nsubsection 19C(1)\nsubsection 10J(1)\nsection 26A\nsection 15\nsubsection 38(2)\nsubsection 12Y(2)\nsubsection 40G(1)\nsubsection 15J(1)\n\nSchedule 2  Application and transitional provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-2-sec-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-2-sec-3-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "faedc43d97acf4249fd6710f7c29da6687daaf6315fa8562bfef667c53404fee",
      "skos:note": "Defines eligible instruments under repealed Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-2-sec-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Effect of instruments made under repealed Part 2",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 98,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nFor the purposes of this item, an eligible instrument means regulations,\na declaration, a determination, a direction, a notice or any other\ninstrument that was:\n\n(a) made or given under a provision (the original provision) of\nPart 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and\nService Standards) Act 1999 in the table in subitem (3), or\nmade or given for the purposes of such a provision; and\n\nApplication and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            95\n\n(b) in force immediately before this Act received the Royal\nAssent.\n(2)\nDespite the repeal and substitution of that Part by Schedule 1 to this\nAct, an eligible instrument has effect, after that Schedule commences,\nas if:\n\n(a) it had been made or given under, or for the purposes of, the\nequivalent provision of that Part in the table in subitem (3);\nand\n\n(b) any requirement for the making or giving of the eligible\ninstrument had been satisfied.\n(3)\nThis table sets out the original provisions, and their equivalent\nprovisions, of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999.\n\nEquivalent provisions of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999\nItem\nThis original provision\n(before this Act receives the\nRoyal Assent):\n... is equivalent, after Schedule 1\ncommences, to this provision:\nsubparagraph 11(b)(iii)\nsubparagraph 9C(b)(iii)\nsection 12\nsection 9D\nsection 13\nsection 9E\nsection 14\nsection 9F\nsubsection 14A(1)\nsubsection 10F(1)\nsubsection 14A(5)\nsubsection 10G(1)\nsection 17\nsubsection 20B(1)\nsection 18\nsection 8F\nsubsection 19(3)\nsubsection 9(3)\nsubsection 19(5)\nsubsection 9A(2)\nsubsection 19A(8)\nsubsection 10D(1)\nsubsection 19B(1)\nsubsection 10H(1)\nsubsection 19C(1)\nsubsection 10J(1)\nsection 26A\nsection 15\nsubsection 38(2)\nsubsection 12Y(2)\nsubsection 40G(1)\nsubsection 15J(1)\n\nSchedule 2  Application and transitional provisions"
    },
    {
