    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-2-sec-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 References to certain terms in eligible instruments",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-2-sec-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.100",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nFor the purposes of this item, an eligible instrument means regulations,\na declaration, a determination, a direction, a notice or any other\ninstrument that:\n\n(a) was in force immediately before this Act received the Royal\nAssent; and\n\n(b) contains a reference to a term the definition of which is\nrepealed by this Act.\n(2)\nFor the purposes of the amendments made by Schedule 1 to this Act,\nthe Minister or the ACA may determine in writing that a specified\neligible instrument has effect, after that Schedule commences, as if a\nreference in the instrument to a specified term were a reference to\nanother specified term.\nNote:\nAn instrument may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class or in any\nother way.",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nFor the purposes of this item, an eligible instrument means regulations,\na declaration, a determination, a direction, a notice or any other\ninstrument that:\n\n(a) was in force immediately before this Act received the Royal\nAssent; and\n\n(b) contains a reference to a term the definition of which is\nrepealed by this Act.\n(2)\nFor the purposes of the amendments made by Schedule 1 to this Act,\nthe Minister or the ACA may determine in writing that a specified\neligible instrument has effect, after that Schedule commences, as if a\nreference in the instrument to a specified term were a reference to\nanother specified term.\nNote:\nAn instrument may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class or in any\nother way.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-2-sec-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1b1e4a41f1222ead826308feef3880067c6fa685b988ba76633faef0a9dbb6f6",
      "skos:note": "Definition of eligible instrument"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-2-sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 References to certain terms in eligible instruments",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 100,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nFor the purposes of this item, an eligible instrument means regulations,\na declaration, a determination, a direction, a notice or any other\ninstrument that:\n\n(a) was in force immediately before this Act received the Royal\nAssent; and\n\n(b) contains a reference to a term the definition of which is\nrepealed by this Act.\n(2)\nFor the purposes of the amendments made by Schedule 1 to this Act,\nthe Minister or the ACA may determine in writing that a specified\neligible instrument has effect, after that Schedule commences, as if a\nreference in the instrument to a specified term were a reference to\nanother specified term.\nNote:\nAn instrument may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class or in any\nother way."
    },
    {
