      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-2-sec-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 Treatment of draft universal service plans",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-2-sec-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.100",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThis item applies to a draft universal service plan given to the Minister\nunder Division 4 of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer\nProtection and Service Standards) Act 1999, that the Minister has\nneither approved nor refused to approve, before this Act received the\nRoyal Assent.\n\nApplication and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            97\n(2)\nTo the extent that the draft contains statements of the policy that the\nuniversal service provider concerned will apply in supplying equipment,\ngoods or services, the draft is, after Schedule 1 to this Act commences,\ntaken to be a draft policy statement for the purposes of the\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act\n1999.\n(3)\nThe remainder of the draft is, after Schedule 1 commences, taken to be\na draft standard marketing plan for the purposes of that Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThis item applies to a draft universal service plan given to the Minister\nunder Division 4 of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer\nProtection and Service Standards) Act 1999, that the Minister has\nneither approved nor refused to approve, before this Act received the\nRoyal Assent.\n\nApplication and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            97\n(2)\nTo the extent that the draft contains statements of the policy that the\nuniversal service provider concerned will apply in supplying equipment,\ngoods or services, the draft is, after Schedule 1 to this Act commences,\ntaken to be a draft policy statement for the purposes of the\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act\n1999.\n(3)\nThe remainder of the draft is, after Schedule 1 commences, taken to be\na draft standard marketing plan for the purposes of that Act.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-2-sec-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-2-sec-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9a32ac212500d178c2b47f22a4533a8257fbd7f678f466a96427b5ed4796835e",
      "skos:note": "The draft universal service plan must be taken to be a policy statement or standard marketing plan after Schedule 1 commences."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-2-sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 Treatment of draft universal service plans",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 100,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThis item applies to a draft universal service plan given to the Minister\nunder Division 4 of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer\nProtection and Service Standards) Act 1999, that the Minister has\nneither approved nor refused to approve, before this Act received the\nRoyal Assent.\n\nApplication and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            97\n(2)\nTo the extent that the draft contains statements of the policy that the\nuniversal service provider concerned will apply in supplying equipment,\ngoods or services, the draft is, after Schedule 1 to this Act commences,\ntaken to be a draft policy statement for the purposes of the\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act\n1999.\n(3)\nThe remainder of the draft is, after Schedule 1 commences, taken to be\na draft standard marketing plan for the purposes of that Act."
    },
    {
