    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-2-sec-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 Treatment of approved universal service plans",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-2-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.101",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThis item applies to an approved universal service plan under\nDivision 4 of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999 that was in force immediately before\nthis Act received the Royal Assent.\n(2)\nTo the extent that the plan contains statements of the policy that the\nuniversal service provider concerned will apply in supplying equipment,\ngoods or services, the plan is, after Schedule 1 to this Act commences,\ntaken to be an approved policy statement for the purposes of the\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act\n1999.\n(3)\nThe remainder of the plan is, after Schedule 1 commences, taken to be\nan approved standard marketing plan for the purposes of that Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThis item applies to an approved universal service plan under\nDivision 4 of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999 that was in force immediately before\nthis Act received the Royal Assent.\n(2)\nTo the extent that the plan contains statements of the policy that the\nuniversal service provider concerned will apply in supplying equipment,\ngoods or services, the plan is, after Schedule 1 to this Act commences,\ntaken to be an approved policy statement for the purposes of the\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act\n1999.\n(3)\nThe remainder of the plan is, after Schedule 1 commences, taken to be\nan approved standard marketing plan for the purposes of that Act.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-2-sec-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-2-sec-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-2-sec-6-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3502484e95e2336c7c03c519de24f6caa27938e09f60447a5aa58230696abe9c",
      "skos:note": "Approved universal service plans must be treated in a certain way after the Act receives Royal Assent."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-2-sec-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 Treatment of approved universal service plans",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 101,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThis item applies to an approved universal service plan under\nDivision 4 of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999 that was in force immediately before\nthis Act received the Royal Assent.\n(2)\nTo the extent that the plan contains statements of the policy that the\nuniversal service provider concerned will apply in supplying equipment,\ngoods or services, the plan is, after Schedule 1 to this Act commences,\ntaken to be an approved policy statement for the purposes of the\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act\n1999.\n(3)\nThe remainder of the plan is, after Schedule 1 commences, taken to be\nan approved standard marketing plan for the purposes of that Act."
    },
