    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-3-sec-101b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "101B Performance bonds and guarantees",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-3-sec-101b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.109",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written determination, require a person who\nhas a liability to pay levy, or an anticipated liability to pay levy,\nunder section 99 to obtain, in accordance with the determination,\nperformance bonds or guarantees in respect of the person’s liability\nor anticipated liability.\n\n(2) The person must comply with the determination.\n\n(3) A determination under this section is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n(4) In this section:\nperformance bond has the meaning given by the determination.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by written determination, require a person who\nhas a liability to pay levy, or an anticipated liability to pay levy,\nunder section 99 to obtain, in accordance with the determination,\nperformance bonds or guarantees in respect of the person’s liability\nor anticipated liability.\n\n(2) The person must comply with the determination.\n\n(3) A determination under this section is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n(4) In this section:\nperformance bond has the meaning given by the determination.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-3-sec-101b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-3-sec-101b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-3-sec-101b-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-3-sec-101b-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d60c7b2e1edb0859838043d527ff94bf7e984b3b3279eb7f03f72b8ec7ce4362"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-3-sec-101b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "101B Performance bonds and guarantees",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 109,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written determination, require a person who\nhas a liability to pay levy, or an anticipated liability to pay levy,\nunder section 99 to obtain, in accordance with the determination,\nperformance bonds or guarantees in respect of the person’s liability\nor anticipated liability.\n\n(2) The person must comply with the determination.\n\n(3) A determination under this section is a disallowable instrument for\nthe purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n(4) In this section:\nperformance bond has the meaning given by the determination."
    },
