      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "the operation of the former law for the 1998-1999 financial year is preserved by item 23 of Schedule 4 to the Telecommunications Legislation Amendment Act 1999.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "payment of levy for the period between the start and end of the 1998-1999 financial year."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-2-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "if",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Conditional obligation with preservation clause",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "item 23 of Schedule 4 to the Telecommunications Legislation Amendment Act 1999 preserves the operation of the former law for the 1998-1999 financial year.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "payment of levy for the period between the start and end of the 1998-1999 financial year if certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Assessment based on estimate of eligible revenue",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-4-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.112",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf a participating carrier fails to give the ACA a return under\nsection 191 of the former law for the 1998-1999 financial year, the\nACA may:\n\n(a) estimate the carrier’s eligible revenue for the year; and\n\n(b) make a written assessment under section 193 of the former\nlaw of the carrier’s eligible revenue for the year based on the\nestimate.\n(2)\nThe ACA must give at least 14 days’ notice to the carrier of the ACA’s\nproposal to make the assessment based on the estimate, and of the\namount of eligible return proposed to be assessed. The notice must be in\nwriting.\n(3)\nThe ACA must not make an assessment based on an estimate after\nreceiving a return for the year from the carrier concerned.\n\nLevy distribution for the 1998-1999 financial year  Schedule 4\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            109\n(4)\nHowever, if the ACA has made an assessment based on the estimate,\nthe ACA is not required to change it if a return is later given to the\nACA.",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nIf a participating carrier fails to give the ACA a return under\nsection 191 of the former law for the 1998-1999 financial year, the\nACA may:\n\n(a) estimate the carrier’s eligible revenue for the year; and\n\n(b) make a written assessment under section 193 of the former\nlaw of the carrier’s eligible revenue for the year based on the\nestimate.\n(2)\nThe ACA must give at least 14 days’ notice to the carrier of the ACA’s\nproposal to make the assessment based on the estimate, and of the\namount of eligible return proposed to be assessed. The notice must be in\nwriting.\n(3)\nThe ACA must not make an assessment based on an estimate after\nreceiving a return for the year from the carrier concerned.\n\nLevy distribution for the 1998-1999 financial year  Schedule 4\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            109\n(4)\nHowever, if the ACA has made an assessment based on the estimate,\nthe ACA is not required to change it if a return is later given to the\nACA.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-3-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-3-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-3-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-3-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "10ba786108618082cc7deaadc2875f8d757aa7cbd265b7eaa7c51bedcf96bfb8",
      "skos:note": "Assessment based on estimate of eligible revenue",
      "dc:description": "Return under section 191 of the former law for the 1998-1999 financial year"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-4-sec-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Assessment based on estimate of eligible revenue",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 112,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf a participating carrier fails to give the ACA a return under\nsection 191 of the former law for the 1998-1999 financial year, the\nACA may:\n\n(a) estimate the carrier’s eligible revenue for the year; and\n\n(b) make a written assessment under section 193 of the former\nlaw of the carrier’s eligible revenue for the year based on the\nestimate.\n(2)\nThe ACA must give at least 14 days’ notice to the carrier of the ACA’s\nproposal to make the assessment based on the estimate, and of the\namount of eligible return proposed to be assessed. The notice must be in\nwriting.\n(3)\nThe ACA must not make an assessment based on an estimate after\nreceiving a return for the year from the carrier concerned.\n\nLevy distribution for the 1998-1999 financial year  Schedule 4\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            109\n(4)\nHowever, if the ACA has made an assessment based on the estimate,\nthe ACA is not required to change it if a return is later given to the\nACA."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
