    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 Working out how much levy is payable",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-4-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.113",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf the total of the amounts payable to carriers out of the Universal\nService Account is more than the balance of the Universal Service\nAccount, after paying any refunds that are due under section 208 of the\nformer law, the ACA must:\n\n(a) work out the amount payable to each carrier as a proportion\nof the total amounts payable; and\n\n(b) ensure that any payments out of the Universal Service\nAccount are made in accordance with those proportions\n(rounding amounts to whole dollars as the ACA considers\nappropriate).\n(2)\nHowever, if the Minister determines in writing a different method for\nmaking payments out of the Universal Service Account than the method\nprovided in subitem (1), the ACA must act in accordance with that\ndetermination.\n\nSchedule 4  Levy distribution for the 1998-1999 financial year",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nIf the total of the amounts payable to carriers out of the Universal\nService Account is more than the balance of the Universal Service\nAccount, after paying any refunds that are due under section 208 of the\nformer law, the ACA must:\n\n(a) work out the amount payable to each carrier as a proportion\nof the total amounts payable; and\n\n(b) ensure that any payments out of the Universal Service\nAccount are made in accordance with those proportions\n(rounding amounts to whole dollars as the ACA considers\nappropriate).\n(2)\nHowever, if the Minister determines in writing a different method for\nmaking payments out of the Universal Service Account than the method\nprovided in subitem (1), the ACA must act in accordance with that\ndetermination.\n\nSchedule 4  Levy distribution for the 1998-1999 financial year",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cd0d707efa3900315ed1ba0b6b8be05b99ab59aff83b1c43989dfee65c565b9e",
      "skos:note": "Ensure payments are made in accordance with proportions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-4-sec-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 Working out how much levy is payable",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 113,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf the total of the amounts payable to carriers out of the Universal\nService Account is more than the balance of the Universal Service\nAccount, after paying any refunds that are due under section 208 of the\nformer law, the ACA must:\n\n(a) work out the amount payable to each carrier as a proportion\nof the total amounts payable; and\n\n(b) ensure that any payments out of the Universal Service\nAccount are made in accordance with those proportions\n(rounding amounts to whole dollars as the ACA considers\nappropriate).\n(2)\nHowever, if the Minister determines in writing a different method for\nmaking payments out of the Universal Service Account than the method\nprovided in subitem (1), the ACA must act in accordance with that\ndetermination.\n\nSchedule 4  Levy distribution for the 1998-1999 financial year"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-6"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
