      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must ensure payments are made in accordance with proportions",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(b)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-110",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "110 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-4-sec-110"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.114",
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n(3)\nA determination under subitem (2) is a disallowable instrument for the\npurposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n(4)\nA carrier’s levy credit balance for the 1998-1999 financial year is\nreduced by the amount (worked out under this item) that is paid to the\ncarrier.\n(5)\nThis item continues to apply until each carrier’s levy credit balance for\nthe year is reduced to nil.\n\nLevy distribution for the 1999-2000 financial year  Schedule 5\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            111",
      "skos:definition": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n(3)\nA determination under subitem (2) is a disallowable instrument for the\npurposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n(4)\nA carrier’s levy credit balance for the 1998-1999 financial year is\nreduced by the amount (worked out under this item) that is paid to the\ncarrier.\n(5)\nThis item continues to apply until each carrier’s levy credit balance for\nthe year is reduced to nil.\n\nLevy distribution for the 1999-2000 financial year  Schedule 5\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            111",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-110-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-110-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e200a79599ebea480aab3fcfe839123295a6d837002512f77f2df5f91bb850e4",
      "skos:note": "Reduces carrier's levy credit balance by amount paid to the carrier."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-4-sec-110",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "110 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 114,
      "values:originalText": "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000\n(3)\nA determination under subitem (2) is a disallowable instrument for the\npurposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n(4)\nA carrier’s levy credit balance for the 1998-1999 financial year is\nreduced by the amount (worked out under this item) that is paid to the\ncarrier.\n(5)\nThis item continues to apply until each carrier’s levy credit balance for\nthe year is reduced to nil.\n\nLevy distribution for the 1999-2000 financial year  Schedule 5\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            111"
    },
    {
