    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-5-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Assessment based on estimate of eligible revenue",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-5-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.115",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf a participating carrier fails to give the ACA a return under section 62\nof the former law for the 1999-2000 financial year, the ACA may:\n\n(a) estimate the carrier’s eligible revenue for the year; and\n\n(b) make a written assessment under section 64 of the former law\nof the carrier’s eligible revenue for the year based on the\nestimate.\n(2)\nThe ACA must give at least 14 days’ notice to the carrier of the ACA’s\nproposal to make the assessment based on the estimate, and of the\namount of eligible return proposed to be assessed. The notice must be in\nwriting.\n(3)\nThe ACA must not make an assessment based on an estimate after\nreceiving a return for the year from the carrier concerned.\n\nSchedule 5  Levy distribution for the 1999-2000 financial year",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nIf a participating carrier fails to give the ACA a return under section 62\nof the former law for the 1999-2000 financial year, the ACA may:\n\n(a) estimate the carrier’s eligible revenue for the year; and\n\n(b) make a written assessment under section 64 of the former law\nof the carrier’s eligible revenue for the year based on the\nestimate.\n(2)\nThe ACA must give at least 14 days’ notice to the carrier of the ACA’s\nproposal to make the assessment based on the estimate, and of the\namount of eligible return proposed to be assessed. The notice must be in\nwriting.\n(3)\nThe ACA must not make an assessment based on an estimate after\nreceiving a return for the year from the carrier concerned.\n\nSchedule 5  Levy distribution for the 1999-2000 financial year",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-5-sec-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-5-sec-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "36ad928e576f164734deda293ab92eb038a6351728402a8f7c1ed10df8e69ceb",
      "skos:note": "The ACA must give at least 14 days' notice to the carrier of the ACA's proposal to make the assessment based on the estimate, and of the amount of eligible return proposed to be assessed.",
      "dc:description": "Notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-5-sec-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Assessment based on estimate of eligible revenue",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 115,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf a participating carrier fails to give the ACA a return under section 62\nof the former law for the 1999-2000 financial year, the ACA may:\n\n(a) estimate the carrier’s eligible revenue for the year; and\n\n(b) make a written assessment under section 64 of the former law\nof the carrier’s eligible revenue for the year based on the\nestimate.\n(2)\nThe ACA must give at least 14 days’ notice to the carrier of the ACA’s\nproposal to make the assessment based on the estimate, and of the\namount of eligible return proposed to be assessed. The notice must be in\nwriting.\n(3)\nThe ACA must not make an assessment based on an estimate after\nreceiving a return for the year from the carrier concerned.\n\nSchedule 5  Levy distribution for the 1999-2000 financial year"
    },
    {
