    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-5-sec-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 Working out how much levy is payable",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-5-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.116",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf the total of the amounts payable to carriers out of the Universal\nService Account is more than the balance of the Universal Service\nAccount, after paying any refunds that are due under section 79 of the\nformer law, the ACA must:\n\n(a) work out the amount payable to each carrier as a proportion\nof the total amounts payable; and\n\n(b) ensure that any payments out of the Universal Service\nAccount are made in accordance with those proportions\n(rounding amounts to whole dollars as the ACA considers\nappropriate).\n(2)\nHowever, if the Minister determines in writing a different method for\nmaking payments out of the Universal Service Account than the method\nprovided in subitem (1), the ACA must act in accordance with that\ndetermination.\n\nLevy distribution for the 1999-2000 financial year  Schedule 5\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            113\n(3)\nA determination under subitem (2) is a disallowable instrument for the\npurposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n(4)\nA carrier’s levy credit balance for the 1999-2000 financial year is\nreduced by the amount (worked out under this item) that is paid to the\ncarrier.\n(5)\nThis item continues to apply until each carrier’s levy credit balance for\nthe year is reduced to nil.\n\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 29 June 2000\nSenate on 11 October 2000]\n\n(133/00)",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nIf the total of the amounts payable to carriers out of the Universal\nService Account is more than the balance of the Universal Service\nAccount, after paying any refunds that are due under section 79 of the\nformer law, the ACA must:\n\n(a) work out the amount payable to each carrier as a proportion\nof the total amounts payable; and\n\n(b) ensure that any payments out of the Universal Service\nAccount are made in accordance with those proportions\n(rounding amounts to whole dollars as the ACA considers\nappropriate).\n(2)\nHowever, if the Minister determines in writing a different method for\nmaking payments out of the Universal Service Account than the method\nprovided in subitem (1), the ACA must act in accordance with that\ndetermination.\n\nLevy distribution for the 1999-2000 financial year  Schedule 5\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000\nNo. 142, 2000            113\n(3)\nA determination under subitem (2) is a disallowable instrument for the\npurposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n(4)\nA carrier’s levy credit balance for the 1999-2000 financial year is\nreduced by the amount (worked out under this item) that is paid to the\ncarrier.\n(5)\nThis item continues to apply until each carrier’s levy credit balance for\nthe year is reduced to nil.\n\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 29 June 2000\nSenate on 11 October 2000]\n\n(133/00)",
